1
00:01:18,684 --> 00:01:21,311
<i>Hi. My name is Peter Parker.</i>

2
00:01:23,355 --> 00:01:26,399
<i>You don't remember me,
but I have something to tell you</i>

3
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:28,402
<i>that's gonna sound crazy.</i>

4
00:01:31,196 --> 00:01:32,406
<i>But it's the truth.</i>

5
00:01:34,283 --> 00:01:36,034
<i>And I know you're gonna believe me,</i>

6
00:01:36,159 --> 00:01:39,288
<i>because you're very good
at telling when I'm lying.</i>

7
00:01:41,081 --> 00:01:43,666
E.V., can you check the calibration
of my targeting matrix?

8
00:01:43,667 --> 00:01:45,376
That doesn't feel zeroed in to me.

9
00:01:45,377 --> 00:01:47,379
<i>Checking target calibration.</i>

10
00:01:56,179 --> 00:01:57,389
Hey, E.V., take five.

11
00:01:58,140 --> 00:01:59,182
<i>Standing by.</i>

12
00:02:04,896 --> 00:02:06,315
<i>We used to know each other.</i>

13
00:02:07,691 --> 00:02:09,483
<i>We were together.</i>

14
00:02:10,736 --> 00:02:12,403
<i>But something bad was gonna happen,</i>

15
00:02:12,404 --> 00:02:15,991
<i>and the only way to stop it
was to make everyone forget me.</i>

16
00:02:20,871 --> 00:02:23,205
{\an8}<i>First day at MIT, let's go!</i>

17
00:02:23,206 --> 00:02:25,334
{\an8}<i>Oh, my gosh! We're here! We made it!</i>

18
00:02:26,084 --> 00:02:27,251
<i>MJ, come on.</i>

19
00:02:27,252 --> 00:02:28,419
{\an8}<i>Including you.</i>

20
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:29,879
{\an8}<i>Pretend like you're not the happiest
you've ever been</i>

21
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:31,256
{\an8}<i>in your entire life right now.</i>

22
00:02:32,215 --> 00:02:33,382
{\an8}<i>I can't.</i>

23
00:02:33,383 --> 00:02:36,260
{\an8}<i>-Let's just do this! You're happy!
- Okay, okay, okay. Okay.</i>

24
00:02:36,261 --> 00:02:38,263
<i>Because I'm not just Peter Parker.</i>

25
00:02:40,015 --> 00:02:41,432
<i>I'm Spider-Man.</i>

26
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:43,225
<i>I'm really, really
understanding the culture</i>

27
00:02:43,226 --> 00:02:44,769
<i>out here in Boston is just so different.</i>

28
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:47,688
<i>And sometimes,
Spider-Man has to do the hard thing,</i>

29
00:02:47,689 --> 00:02:49,774
<i>even if it breaks Peter Parker's heart.</i>

30
00:02:49,775 --> 00:02:52,986
<i>And everyone here is like,
"Pahk the cah by the hahba."</i>

31
00:02:54,321 --> 00:02:56,239
<i>And maybe that's my responsibility.</i>

32
00:02:57,407 --> 00:02:58,909
<i>To live alone with the truth.</i>

33
00:03:00,327 --> 00:03:03,830
<i>But the truth is, MJ, that I love you.</i>

34
00:03:05,374 --> 00:03:06,624
<i>And I hope that deep down,</i>

35
00:03:06,625 --> 00:03:09,336
<i>something inside of you
remembers that you love me, too.</i>

36
00:03:10,712 --> 00:03:13,464
<i>Suspect is 5'8", 5'10", medium build.</i>

37
00:03:13,465 --> 00:03:16,259
<i>But until then,
I'm just gonna be Spider-Man.</i>

38
00:03:22,265 --> 00:03:23,308
Incoming!

39
00:03:26,645 --> 00:03:27,646
Hey, get him!

40
00:03:29,064 --> 00:03:30,065
Hey, hey, hey. Whoa, whoa, whoa!

41
00:03:43,412 --> 00:03:45,496
<i>Members of the Manfredi crime syndicate</i>

42
00:03:45,497 --> 00:03:48,125
<i>were apprehended by Spider-Man yesterday.</i>

43
00:04:10,272 --> 00:04:12,566
Hey, we live on the same floor.

44
00:04:14,568 --> 00:04:15,569
Cool.

45
00:04:19,281 --> 00:04:20,866
Does anybody ever come up here?

46
00:04:21,491 --> 00:04:23,577
Not unless they like asbestos.

47
00:04:24,077 --> 00:04:26,788
We've just been using it for storage.

48
00:04:27,831 --> 00:04:29,207
It's perfect.

49
00:04:30,709 --> 00:04:33,211
<i>Hey, everyone, sophomore-year Ned is back.</i>

50
00:04:33,712 --> 00:04:36,548
{\an8}<i>Older, wiser, flyer.</i>

51
00:04:37,382 --> 00:04:38,675
{\an8}<i>Let's go!</i>

52
00:04:39,426 --> 00:04:41,886
{\an8}<i>-What is on your face?
- How do you feel about it?</i>

53
00:04:41,887 --> 00:04:44,014
{\an8}<i>I mean, you look
like an assistant coach.</i>

54
00:04:48,685 --> 00:04:50,437
You sure you wanna do this, Scorpion?

55
00:04:50,812 --> 00:04:52,022
Did you miss me, Spidey?

56
00:04:58,195 --> 00:04:59,612
If I drop you from here,

57
00:04:59,613 --> 00:05:01,823
how long you think
it will take you to hit the ground?

58
00:05:02,866 --> 00:05:04,326
Well, I don't know. You tell me.

59
00:05:05,661 --> 00:05:06,870
Let's end this on a high note, huh?

60
00:05:13,168 --> 00:05:14,294
Yo, Lonnie!

61
00:05:14,962 --> 00:05:16,170
{\an8}Wha ha happened?

62
00:05:16,171 --> 00:05:19,799
{\an8}DeWolff, all the evidence you're gonna
need is in the trunk of his car.

63
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,009
You tryin' to take my job, Spider-Man?

64
00:05:22,010 --> 00:05:24,304
Hey, you guys are the professionals,
I'm just a volunteer.

65
00:05:34,773 --> 00:05:36,857
<i>It's a new New York.</i>

66
00:05:36,858 --> 00:05:40,528
<i>Thanks to Spider-Man,
crime rates have dropped to a record low.</i>

67
00:05:40,529 --> 00:05:42,989
<i>Police and Damage Control
give much of the credit</i>

68
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:44,156
<i>to the masked hero.</i>

69
00:05:44,157 --> 00:05:45,574
Initiate HUD test.

70
00:05:45,575 --> 00:05:47,702
<i>Armed robbery at Civic Union Bank.</i>

71
00:05:47,703 --> 00:05:49,745
<i>In the past six months,
he has taken down</i>

72
00:05:49,746 --> 00:05:52,790
<i>every major crime lord
across the five boroughs,</i>

73
00:05:52,791 --> 00:05:56,253
<i>including the superpowered
ninja group The Hand.</i>

74
00:06:00,132 --> 00:06:01,841
{\an8}<i>He is the pride of New York City.</i>

75
00:06:01,842 --> 00:06:06,138
{\an8}<i>The hero every grown-up relies on
and every kid wants to be.</i>

76
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:09,640
<i>Final semester, MIT.</i>

77
00:06:09,641 --> 00:06:11,935
{\an8}<i>Oh, my gosh, we're graduating in a month.</i>

78
00:06:12,352 --> 00:06:15,646
<i>We've made so many memories.
Where do I begin?</i>

79
00:06:15,647 --> 00:06:18,899
<i>Night swimming in the Charles River
with Jim and Wiley.</i>

80
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:21,777
<i>The infamous food fight
at the Banana Lounge.</i>

81
00:06:21,778 --> 00:06:26,157
<i>Pulling all-nighters in Stud 5
with MJ and Nate Dawg.</i>

82
00:06:26,158 --> 00:06:28,993
<i>It feels like yesterday
I was sitting on a roof with MJ,</i>

83
00:06:28,994 --> 00:06:32,413
<i>dreaming about coming here together,
and I still can't believe we did it.</i>

84
00:06:32,414 --> 00:06:35,207
<i>I'm so grateful
for all the friends that I've made.</i>

85
00:06:35,208 --> 00:06:37,627
<i>I couldn't imagine
going through this with anyone else.</i>

86
00:06:37,628 --> 00:06:39,712
{\an8}<i>Ned, who do you think
is actually watching these?</i>

87
00:06:39,713 --> 00:06:42,340
{\an8}<i>-I don't know. But maybe someone.
- Okay.</i>

88
00:06:42,341 --> 00:06:43,716
{\an8}<i>Okay, well, bye, someone.</i>

89
00:06:43,717 --> 00:06:45,802
{\an8}<i>-What? No!
- Bye. We're done. Yeah, we're done.</i>

90
00:07:03,904 --> 00:07:07,198
I mean, we're talking about
downtown Brooklyn in broad daylight.

91
00:07:07,199 --> 00:07:10,201
High-profile job like that,
you know that Foswell was involved.

92
00:07:10,202 --> 00:07:12,495
Yeah, I hear you, but can you prove it?

93
00:07:12,496 --> 00:07:14,455
Yeah, I'm going through
his financial records

94
00:07:14,456 --> 00:07:15,958
and I'm following his crew every night.

95
00:07:16,875 --> 00:07:19,043
<i>Do you do anything besides work?</i>

96
00:07:19,044 --> 00:07:20,670
You know the saying,
"You do something you love,

97
00:07:20,671 --> 00:07:21,922
"you don't work a day in your life."

98
00:07:23,507 --> 00:07:25,591
- Mom, where's my calculator?
- I don't know.

99
00:07:25,592 --> 00:07:29,637
<i>Trust me, aight?
Being married to the job never ends well.</i>

100
00:07:29,638 --> 00:07:31,722
Well, don't worry about it. I'll be okay.

101
00:07:31,723 --> 00:07:34,351
Oh, yeah?
You still getting them headaches, though?

102
00:07:35,769 --> 00:07:38,270
Yeah. But... But I'll be fine.

103
00:07:38,271 --> 00:07:39,522
<i>I don't know, man.</i>

104
00:07:39,523 --> 00:07:41,607
<i>I think your body's tryin'
to tell you somethin'.</i>

105
00:07:41,608 --> 00:07:44,151
Like you need to get outta that suit
every once in a while.

106
00:07:44,152 --> 00:07:46,112
Mom, do you know where my calculator is?

107
00:07:46,113 --> 00:07:47,114
I don't know, <i>Papi.</i>

108
00:07:47,572 --> 00:07:50,449
<i>What you need
is some real human connection.</i>

109
00:07:50,450 --> 00:07:52,159
What? And we're not connecting?

110
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:56,956
<i>Nah, dude. I don't know your name,
your face, or nothing about you.</i>

111
00:07:56,957 --> 00:07:59,417
I don't think you've ever asked me
a question about my life.

112
00:07:59,418 --> 00:08:00,501
<i>Sure, I have.</i>

113
00:08:00,502 --> 00:08:01,878
<i>Yeah, what are my kids' names?</i>

114
00:08:02,504 --> 00:08:04,506
Well, for starters,
your son's name's <i>Papi.</i>

115
00:08:06,258 --> 00:08:07,425
Is it Spider-Man?

116
00:08:07,426 --> 00:08:09,344
I can't tell you that, sweetheart.

117
00:08:09,803 --> 00:08:11,304
That means it's Spider-Man.

118
00:08:11,305 --> 00:08:12,472
Gosh.

119
00:08:15,142 --> 00:08:18,144
<i>A hijacked tank is heading southbound
past 34th Street.</i>

120
00:08:18,145 --> 00:08:19,563
<i>All available units respond.</i>

121
00:08:19,896 --> 00:08:21,063
Hey, you getting this?

122
00:08:21,064 --> 00:08:22,898
More work. Lucky you.

123
00:08:22,899 --> 00:08:24,108
Okay, I'll see you out there.

124
00:08:24,109 --> 00:08:25,235
I'm so sorry, I gotta go.

125
00:09:42,604 --> 00:09:43,980
I got you, Spidey!

126
00:09:43,981 --> 00:09:45,274
No, no. I don't need your...

127
00:09:59,621 --> 00:10:00,664
Hey! Heads up!

128
00:10:02,499 --> 00:10:05,711
You okay, kid? Yeah, you're okay.
See ya later.

129
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:11,882
You wouldn't know it
just by looking at it,

130
00:10:11,883 --> 00:10:15,887
{\an8}but this very street was completely
destroyed in the Battle of New York.

131
00:10:23,228 --> 00:10:24,938
Come on, come on, come on.

132
00:10:26,607 --> 00:10:28,483
Come on.

133
00:10:41,413 --> 00:10:42,414
Oh, God.

134
00:10:51,131 --> 00:10:52,132
Come on.

135
00:10:52,591 --> 00:10:53,592
Hey.

136
00:10:55,093 --> 00:10:57,136
The hell, Frank?
You just hit me with the van!

137
00:10:57,137 --> 00:10:58,512
Quit your whimpering.

138
00:10:58,513 --> 00:11:00,139
We're not doing that again, Frank.

139
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:01,641
You're goddamn right we're not.

140
00:11:01,642 --> 00:11:03,393
This time you're gonna
get the hell outta my way.

141
00:11:03,894 --> 00:11:05,354
You mean instead of saving your life?

142
00:11:06,313 --> 00:11:08,814
You gonna talk about
that Staten Island bullshit again?

143
00:11:08,815 --> 00:11:10,524
Well, you said it, not me.

144
00:11:10,525 --> 00:11:11,609
Jeez.

145
00:11:11,610 --> 00:11:13,653
Look, man, you can't just shoot yourself
out of every situation.

146
00:11:13,654 --> 00:11:15,112
Innocent people get hurt.

147
00:11:15,113 --> 00:11:17,407
Who do you think's downrange of that tank,
dumb-dumb?

148
00:11:22,913 --> 00:11:23,914
Suit yourself.

149
00:11:27,584 --> 00:11:28,585
Jackass.

150
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:30,754
This freakin' guy.

151
00:11:44,601 --> 00:11:45,602
Motherf...

152
00:11:46,853 --> 00:11:48,146
Go home, Frank!

153
00:11:52,734 --> 00:11:54,236
I'm gonna kill this kid.

154
00:11:59,074 --> 00:12:01,450
- DeWolff?
- Are you gonna stop that thing or what?

155
00:12:01,451 --> 00:12:04,161
<i>It's heading straight
for the Damage Control Detention Center.</i>

156
00:12:04,162 --> 00:12:05,246
I'm trying.

157
00:12:05,247 --> 00:12:06,372
<i>Try harder.</i>

158
00:12:06,373 --> 00:12:08,207
<i>There's a lot of scary dudes
locked up in there.</i>

159
00:12:08,208 --> 00:12:09,751
Well, who do you think put them in there?

160
00:12:10,711 --> 00:12:13,964
Let's go, Scorpion. Moving day.

161
00:12:41,450 --> 00:12:43,243
Please! Evac now!

162
00:12:44,202 --> 00:12:46,997
All right, everybody, clear out!
This guy is armed and dangerous.

163
00:12:59,259 --> 00:13:00,761
Get out of the vehicle, ma'am.

164
00:13:01,386 --> 00:13:03,221
I was thinking the same thing.

165
00:13:12,022 --> 00:13:13,482
Spider-Man?

166
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:15,943
Where am I?

167
00:13:23,075 --> 00:13:24,159
What the...

168
00:13:26,745 --> 00:13:28,371
Move! Move! Move! Move! Move!

169
00:13:28,372 --> 00:13:30,123
Keep her for questioning.
Clear the building.

170
00:13:33,293 --> 00:13:35,294
Enjoy the ride, Scorpion!

171
00:13:35,295 --> 00:13:37,923
You won't be seeing much daylight
in supermax.

172
00:13:38,966 --> 00:13:40,968
Scorpions are nocturnal, buddy.

173
00:13:43,887 --> 00:13:47,265
<i>The building is under attack.
Get the prisoner out of here now!</i>

174
00:13:52,437 --> 00:13:53,438
Sir!

175
00:14:12,207 --> 00:14:13,833
You gotta take off now!

176
00:14:13,834 --> 00:14:15,836
The building has been breached. Go! Go!

177
00:14:16,253 --> 00:14:18,839
Hey, fire it up! Go! Go!

178
00:14:27,264 --> 00:14:28,473
Change of plans!

179
00:14:29,057 --> 00:14:30,934
Take him to the helipad at Bellevue.

180
00:14:31,685 --> 00:14:33,436
- What?
- That's an order

181
00:14:33,437 --> 00:14:34,979
from Director Metzger. Go!

182
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:36,105
Now!

183
00:14:36,106 --> 00:14:37,149
Copy that.

184
00:14:48,118 --> 00:14:49,869
Hey! What...

185
00:14:49,870 --> 00:14:51,288
How did I get up here?

186
00:14:55,584 --> 00:14:58,587
Spider-Man, save me, would you?

187
00:15:04,301 --> 00:15:05,302
Who are you?

188
00:15:06,553 --> 00:15:08,095
You can see me.

189
00:15:08,096 --> 00:15:09,431
Tell me who you are.

190
00:15:10,682 --> 00:15:11,683
You first.

191
00:15:14,770 --> 00:15:16,939
Hey. Hey.

192
00:15:22,819 --> 00:15:24,071
You pushed me out.

193
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:26,030
Interesting.

194
00:15:26,031 --> 00:15:27,615
What the hell was that?

195
00:15:27,616 --> 00:15:29,784
Did you just try to jump into my mind?

196
00:15:29,785 --> 00:15:32,871
You know, the whole time
you've been chasing me,

197
00:15:33,622 --> 00:15:36,291
you forgot to ask yourself
a very important question.

198
00:15:38,168 --> 00:15:39,461
What's in the tank?

199
00:15:41,421 --> 00:15:43,006
Go! Move.

200
00:15:57,187 --> 00:15:58,188
Spider-Man?

201
00:15:59,398 --> 00:16:00,565
What just happened?

202
00:16:03,527 --> 00:16:04,569
I don't know.

203
00:16:06,738 --> 00:16:07,822
Hey, good job.

204
00:16:07,823 --> 00:16:08,990
Hey, way to go, Spidey.

205
00:16:08,991 --> 00:16:10,783
You guys okay? You good?

206
00:16:10,784 --> 00:16:13,786
I swear. All the things they said I did,
I don't remember doing any of them.

207
00:16:13,787 --> 00:16:15,955
It's okay, it's okay. Look, let these
people take good care of you.

208
00:16:15,956 --> 00:16:17,123
I would never hurt you.

209
00:16:17,124 --> 00:16:18,541
- Okay.
- I love you, Spider-Man.

210
00:16:18,542 --> 00:16:20,084
Yeah. All right, buddy. All right.

211
00:16:20,085 --> 00:16:22,253
- Hey, what do you got?
- Here, get this.

212
00:16:22,254 --> 00:16:24,005
Chopper took Scorpion to Bellevue.

213
00:16:24,006 --> 00:16:26,424
Ten minutes later,
a guard walked him right out the door.

214
00:16:26,425 --> 00:16:27,426
What?

215
00:16:27,759 --> 00:16:28,926
What about the tank?

216
00:16:28,927 --> 00:16:31,637
Stolen from the Damage Control
warehouse in Brooklyn.

217
00:16:31,638 --> 00:16:33,889
Driver was a janitor who worked there.

218
00:16:33,890 --> 00:16:34,974
You got a motive?

219
00:16:34,975 --> 00:16:37,226
<i>Nada.</i> And no criminal record.

220
00:16:37,227 --> 00:16:39,229
Scorpion must've gotten to her somehow.

221
00:16:40,272 --> 00:16:42,148
Yeah. Maybe.

222
00:16:42,149 --> 00:16:43,733
What do you mean, "maybe"?

223
00:16:43,734 --> 00:16:45,652
I mean, I... I don't know.

224
00:16:46,445 --> 00:16:47,862
But I know someone that might.

225
00:16:47,863 --> 00:16:49,030
Where you going?

226
00:16:49,031 --> 00:16:50,781
You keep following the leads on Scorpion.

227
00:16:50,782 --> 00:16:52,451
I'm gonna go talk to someone.

228
00:17:08,008 --> 00:17:11,511
Hi, is this 3250 Brighton Beach?

229
00:17:16,141 --> 00:17:17,267
Okay.

230
00:17:17,976 --> 00:17:19,770
I think I know what that means.

231
00:17:24,857 --> 00:17:26,026
Take off your clothes.

232
00:17:29,112 --> 00:17:30,113
What?

233
00:17:30,572 --> 00:17:32,532
You don't wear clothes in the <i>banya.</i>

234
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,993
Ditch the leotard.

235
00:17:36,161 --> 00:17:37,537
This is not a leotard.

236
00:17:38,372 --> 00:17:40,332
Your text said that this was your office.

237
00:17:41,667 --> 00:17:43,210
This is my office.

238
00:17:43,961 --> 00:17:44,962
Get in.

239
00:17:46,213 --> 00:17:47,631
I'm fine, thanks. I'll just...

240
00:17:48,924 --> 00:17:50,383
My office, my rules.

241
00:17:50,384 --> 00:17:54,345
This way, you get to enjoy
a nice, relaxing soak,

242
00:17:54,346 --> 00:17:56,722
and I get to see that
you don't have any weapons,

243
00:17:56,723 --> 00:17:57,933
and we both win.

244
00:18:00,102 --> 00:18:01,103
Okay.

245
00:18:10,404 --> 00:18:12,947
Really? What, you never take that off?

246
00:18:12,948 --> 00:18:15,033
No, I... You know, it defeats
the whole anonymous thing.

247
00:18:15,242 --> 00:18:19,705
Even for your girlfriend
or boyfriend or whatever?

248
00:18:20,372 --> 00:18:21,999
There's a lot of conjecture online.

249
00:18:22,791 --> 00:18:25,335
And super graphic artwork. Have you seen?

250
00:18:25,544 --> 00:18:28,337
The one with you
and the ten Mysterios, it's...

251
00:18:28,338 --> 00:18:30,673
I've... I've... I've seen it. I've...

252
00:18:30,674 --> 00:18:32,216
It's hard to unsee, to be honest.

253
00:18:32,217 --> 00:18:34,261
But, look, I don't have anyone.
I just kinda keep to myself.

254
00:18:35,053 --> 00:18:36,637
All by yourself? All the time?

255
00:18:36,638 --> 00:18:38,306
No wonder you're so sad.

256
00:18:38,307 --> 00:18:40,558
- I'm not so sad.
- A little bit.

257
00:18:40,559 --> 00:18:42,601
Could we just talk about
what I came here to talk to you about,

258
00:18:42,602 --> 00:18:44,020
the attack on Damage Control?

259
00:18:44,021 --> 00:18:47,816
Yes. So, that is more your area.

260
00:18:48,650 --> 00:18:51,028
Like, small potato stuff.

261
00:18:51,653 --> 00:18:57,743
Whereas the New Avengers
are focusing on big potato stuff.

262
00:18:58,785 --> 00:19:02,289
Right, okay. Well, there's
more to it than that, you know, the...

263
00:19:02,998 --> 00:19:05,541
the driver and the others
who were helping,

264
00:19:05,542 --> 00:19:08,127
it was like someone
was talking to me through them.

265
00:19:08,128 --> 00:19:10,630
Like someone was looking at me
through their eyes.

266
00:19:10,631 --> 00:19:12,923
And you're wondering if it's mind control?

267
00:19:12,924 --> 00:19:15,593
- Exactly.
- Like how they used on me in the Red Room?

268
00:19:15,594 --> 00:19:17,303
- Exactly.
- And the other widows?

269
00:19:17,304 --> 00:19:19,347
- Right.
- Right. No, I don't think so.

270
00:19:19,348 --> 00:19:23,560
I actually think it's probably
more like possession.

271
00:19:24,102 --> 00:19:25,103
Possession?

272
00:19:26,396 --> 00:19:28,397
Like a ghost or a demon.

273
00:19:28,398 --> 00:19:30,191
- Oh, man.
- Or in Russia, we have leshy.

274
00:19:30,192 --> 00:19:33,820
Leshy rules the forest and can possess...

275
00:19:36,281 --> 00:19:37,282
Sorry.

276
00:19:37,824 --> 00:19:40,034
Whatever it is,
they are looking for something.

277
00:19:40,035 --> 00:19:43,538
This is the fourth attack
on the Damage Control facility this month.

278
00:19:44,373 --> 00:19:46,040
And what do you think they're looking for?

279
00:19:46,041 --> 00:19:47,333
I don't know.

280
00:19:47,334 --> 00:19:48,918
But you know what?

281
00:19:48,919 --> 00:19:51,087
After the attack today,

282
00:19:51,088 --> 00:19:55,050
there was a cross-agency cybersecurity
alert that got triggered.

283
00:19:55,509 --> 00:19:58,970
Someone accessed
the Damage Control restricted servers

284
00:19:58,971 --> 00:20:02,473
using credentials from 30 employees
from the way station.

285
00:20:02,474 --> 00:20:04,851
They all searched for the same thing.

286
00:20:06,186 --> 00:20:07,229
V-Max.

287
00:20:09,022 --> 00:20:10,315
V-Max.

288
00:20:11,483 --> 00:20:12,984
Well, what does that mean?

289
00:20:12,985 --> 00:20:15,820
I mean, it could be alien tech,

290
00:20:15,821 --> 00:20:19,573
or secretive weapon programs,

291
00:20:19,574 --> 00:20:22,828
or launch codes or...

292
00:20:24,204 --> 00:20:26,372
I don't know,
this is for you to figure out.

293
00:20:26,373 --> 00:20:29,166
- This is small, baby potato stuff...
- Okay, okay.

294
00:20:29,167 --> 00:20:31,335
- ...not big potato brain stuff.
- You don't have to shout about it. Jeez.

295
00:20:31,336 --> 00:20:33,297
Maybe I'll just go ask
Damage Control myself.

296
00:20:35,882 --> 00:20:38,801
You know, you're not
completely anonymous anymore.

297
00:20:38,802 --> 00:20:40,554
I've seen your belly button.

298
00:20:41,763 --> 00:20:43,974
- Okay.
- Bye.

299
00:21:08,790 --> 00:21:09,875
Oh, God.

300
00:21:11,251 --> 00:21:12,918
Hi, I got an appointment with...

301
00:21:12,919 --> 00:21:14,295
Director Metzger. Yes.

302
00:21:14,296 --> 00:21:15,797
Please step through the scanner.

303
00:21:18,717 --> 00:21:20,719
<i>Enhanced human detected.</i>

304
00:21:21,428 --> 00:21:23,471
<i>Superior strength.</i>

305
00:21:23,472 --> 00:21:25,598
<i>Superior agility.</i>

306
00:21:25,599 --> 00:21:27,308
<i>Heightened senses.</i>

307
00:21:27,309 --> 00:21:29,603
<i>Exogenous DNA. Arachnid.</i>

308
00:21:31,104 --> 00:21:33,439
Please remove your face covering
for identity scan.

309
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:34,732
Oh, no, I can't do that.

310
00:21:34,733 --> 00:21:36,859
- That's not possible.
- Failure to remove your face covering

311
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:38,861
will result in defensive measures.

312
00:21:38,862 --> 00:21:40,697
Defensive measures? What are you talk...

313
00:21:41,823 --> 00:21:44,241
Guys, guys, guys!
I can't take my mask off. I'm...

314
00:21:44,242 --> 00:21:45,285
Spider-Man.

315
00:21:46,370 --> 00:21:47,829
He's all right. At ease.

316
00:21:53,001 --> 00:21:54,961
My apologies.

317
00:21:54,962 --> 00:21:56,171
We are so glad you're here.

318
00:21:56,713 --> 00:21:59,423
Bill Metzger, Director of Damage Control.
How are you?

319
00:21:59,424 --> 00:22:00,467
I'm good, thank you.

320
00:22:01,009 --> 00:22:03,761
We had to beef up security around here,
but I hope we didn't give you a fright.

321
00:22:03,762 --> 00:22:05,931
- No, not at all.
- All right, come on. This way.

322
00:22:07,599 --> 00:22:09,893
This floor is mostly
research and administrative.

323
00:22:10,477 --> 00:22:13,981
Downstairs, we have incident cleanup,
laboratories, agent training.

324
00:22:15,565 --> 00:22:17,276
- Hey, what are they doing here?
- It's okay.

325
00:22:18,235 --> 00:22:19,820
The Hand works for us now.

326
00:22:20,362 --> 00:22:22,113
After you brought them in,
I realized that

327
00:22:22,114 --> 00:22:24,699
fundamentally, they're a group of kids
without a leader.

328
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:26,701
All they needed was a little direction.

329
00:22:26,702 --> 00:22:28,661
Then, suddenly,
all the things that made them dangerous

330
00:22:28,662 --> 00:22:31,039
turned them into an invaluable part
of our security team.

331
00:22:36,712 --> 00:22:39,464
You can look at the many threats
that face us and see only danger.

332
00:22:40,841 --> 00:22:42,301
Or you can see opportunity.

333
00:22:43,885 --> 00:22:44,886
Okay.

334
00:22:49,433 --> 00:22:50,726
Wow, look at that.

335
00:22:51,518 --> 00:22:53,687
In the hands of Shocker,
these are a nuisance.

336
00:22:55,897 --> 00:22:57,690
But it doesn't mean
we can't learn from the technology,

337
00:22:57,691 --> 00:22:59,151
or respect the innovation.

338
00:23:00,068 --> 00:23:04,155
Our mission is to redirect destructive
energy into something useful.

339
00:23:04,156 --> 00:23:05,824
That's the true meaning of Damage Control.

340
00:23:11,204 --> 00:23:12,414
Be careful with that.

341
00:23:13,332 --> 00:23:14,333
Right this way.

342
00:23:17,836 --> 00:23:20,881
I wanted to talk to you
about the recent attacks on the agency.

343
00:23:21,340 --> 00:23:23,257
There's been four, right?

344
00:23:23,258 --> 00:23:24,343
Please have a seat.

345
00:23:25,469 --> 00:23:26,887
You are right.

346
00:23:27,387 --> 00:23:29,890
It appears we're faced with a threat
we can't control.

347
00:23:30,432 --> 00:23:31,516
One we can't even see.

348
00:23:34,311 --> 00:23:35,520
But you can.

349
00:23:36,396 --> 00:23:38,023
I saw the security footage.

350
00:23:39,483 --> 00:23:41,610
I also read Detective DeWolff's report.

351
00:23:42,653 --> 00:23:45,072
I believe you understand
exactly what we're up against.

352
00:23:45,948 --> 00:23:48,951
Someone or something
that can hop into people's minds.

353
00:23:49,993 --> 00:23:51,077
But not yours.

354
00:23:51,078 --> 00:23:53,789
No, I mean, it tried, but it couldn't.

355
00:24:02,965 --> 00:24:04,508
I'm gonna be honest with you.

356
00:24:05,384 --> 00:24:06,677
We're on our heels right now.

357
00:24:07,844 --> 00:24:10,721
God forbid if it were to get in here
and find whatever it is it's looking for,

358
00:24:10,722 --> 00:24:14,434
the consequences could be unimaginable.

359
00:24:17,229 --> 00:24:20,190
Well, let me guess, is whatever
it's looking for in that giant vault?

360
00:24:23,151 --> 00:24:25,486
There are some things,
because of the nature of my job

361
00:24:25,487 --> 00:24:26,738
I cannot tell you.

362
00:24:27,239 --> 00:24:29,700
But I believe you are our
best defense against this.

363
00:24:30,117 --> 00:24:31,618
You're the only one who can sense it.

364
00:24:32,119 --> 00:24:33,537
You're the only one who's immune to it.

365
00:24:34,162 --> 00:24:35,789
I'm counting on you to defeat it.

366
00:24:39,334 --> 00:24:41,420
That's a pretty good speech, Director.

367
00:24:42,170 --> 00:24:43,588
I'll do everything that I can, I promise.

368
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:47,717
Well, then consider yourself
a friend of Damage Control.

369
00:24:47,718 --> 00:24:48,719
Thank you.

370
00:24:49,678 --> 00:24:50,679
I'll be in touch.

371
00:24:52,597 --> 00:24:53,640
I wanted to ask...

372
00:24:54,975 --> 00:24:57,561
the phrase "V-Max"
doesn't mean anything to you, does it?

373
00:24:59,062 --> 00:25:01,440
No. Where'd you hear that?

374
00:25:01,940 --> 00:25:04,859
It's just, you know,
nature of being a superhero,

375
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:06,194
there are some things
I just can't tell ya.

376
00:25:07,529 --> 00:25:08,822
Anyway, I'll see you later.

377
00:25:09,865 --> 00:25:11,366
You guys are doing great. Keep it up.

378
00:25:11,783 --> 00:25:13,951
<i>I don't think Metzger knows
any more than we do,</i>

379
00:25:13,952 --> 00:25:16,078
<i>but I told him
I'd do whatever I can to help.</i>

380
00:25:16,079 --> 00:25:18,539
You wanna help?
The best thing you could do

381
00:25:18,540 --> 00:25:20,750
<i>is find Scorpion.
He's our only lead.</i>

382
00:25:20,751 --> 00:25:22,627
Yeah, I know.
I have every camera in the city

383
00:25:22,628 --> 00:25:24,504
running a facial recognition scan for him.

384
00:25:25,047 --> 00:25:28,424
That sounds super illegal, Spider-Man.
I'mma pretend I didn't hear that.

385
00:25:28,425 --> 00:25:29,884
Yeah, probably for the best.

386
00:25:29,885 --> 00:25:31,427
But look, if he shows his face,
we'll know.

387
00:25:31,428 --> 00:25:32,929
Do you have any mini-kegs?

388
00:25:33,722 --> 00:25:34,972
Down at the end.

389
00:25:34,973 --> 00:25:35,974
Thanks.

390
00:25:39,227 --> 00:25:40,354
I'll call you back.

391
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:46,401
Easy.

392
00:25:50,572 --> 00:25:54,075
Hey, also, you got any Sharkfire Energy?

393
00:25:54,076 --> 00:25:55,452
Yeah.

394
00:25:56,620 --> 00:25:57,995
{\an8}Oh, no, no, no.

395
00:25:57,996 --> 00:25:59,790
I don't want any.
That stuff will kill you.

396
00:26:00,207 --> 00:26:01,916
You know, all my friends
were drinking them during finals

397
00:26:01,917 --> 00:26:03,167
and now they're addicted.

398
00:26:03,168 --> 00:26:06,253
And so I'm gonna need you
to not sell me any.

399
00:26:06,254 --> 00:26:07,422
Memorize my face.

400
00:26:08,590 --> 00:26:12,135
Please do not sell this guy any Sharkfire.

401
00:26:13,011 --> 00:26:14,179
Sure. Whatever.

402
00:26:15,138 --> 00:26:16,348
Actually, I'll take one.

403
00:26:17,099 --> 00:26:18,349
Last one.

404
00:26:18,350 --> 00:26:19,809
Maybe two.

405
00:26:19,810 --> 00:26:21,937
And then never sell me any.

406
00:26:23,522 --> 00:26:24,523
Damn it.

407
00:26:58,724 --> 00:26:59,974
Yo, Ned!

408
00:26:59,975 --> 00:27:01,350
- What?
- Ned!

409
00:27:01,351 --> 00:27:03,060
- Give me that.
- My guy, appreciate you.

410
00:27:03,061 --> 00:27:04,687
- Let's go!
- Yeah, man.

411
00:27:04,688 --> 00:27:05,689
Let's go!

412
00:27:40,307 --> 00:27:43,059
You need a drink.
Take this, take this, take it.

413
00:27:43,060 --> 00:27:44,061
Thanks.

414
00:27:47,230 --> 00:27:48,231
Excuse me.

415
00:28:35,821 --> 00:28:37,698
See you've stumbled across my board.

416
00:28:38,699 --> 00:28:40,200
I'm not one of those weirdos, I swear.

417
00:28:40,784 --> 00:28:43,120
He actually saved me and my friends' lives
a few times in high school.

418
00:28:44,538 --> 00:28:46,163
- Cool.
- Yeah, yeah.

419
00:28:46,164 --> 00:28:48,542
And ever since, I've just been trying
to figure out who he is.

420
00:28:48,834 --> 00:28:53,129
Not to unmask him to the world
or anything, just to know, you know?

421
00:28:53,130 --> 00:28:55,424
And to, hopefully, thank him face to face.

422
00:28:57,926 --> 00:29:01,263
I actually created this app
that monitors his sightings.

423
00:29:01,596 --> 00:29:03,222
Wait, you created Spidey Tracker?

424
00:29:03,223 --> 00:29:04,891
You heard of it? Nice.

425
00:29:05,892 --> 00:29:07,560
{\an8}<i>Where is Spider-Man?</i>

426
00:29:07,561 --> 00:29:08,770
{\an8}Little chat room right there.

427
00:29:09,730 --> 00:29:12,315
Now, we know he's definitely from Queens.

428
00:29:12,316 --> 00:29:13,525
Not the biggest revelation.

429
00:29:14,026 --> 00:29:18,655
But I have been able to narrow it down
to two prime suspects.

430
00:29:22,659 --> 00:29:26,037
Yeah, if you knew who they were,
it would really blow your mind.

431
00:29:26,038 --> 00:29:27,039
I'm sure.

432
00:29:27,831 --> 00:29:28,832
Ned, by the way.

433
00:29:29,875 --> 00:29:30,876
I'm...

434
00:29:31,376 --> 00:29:33,461
God, there's, like,
50 people in our apartment.

435
00:29:33,462 --> 00:29:36,298
Statistically speaking, that means
at least two of them are sociopaths,

436
00:29:36,715 --> 00:29:38,175
which is kind of cool.

437
00:29:41,053 --> 00:29:42,054
Nice flowers.

438
00:29:43,555 --> 00:29:46,682
They're a housewarming gift.

439
00:29:46,683 --> 00:29:47,726
- Really?
- Yeah.

440
00:29:48,435 --> 00:29:50,645
Okay. Most people just brought
beer and chips.

441
00:29:50,646 --> 00:29:51,938
That's very nice.

442
00:29:51,939 --> 00:29:52,981
I'm MJ.

443
00:29:54,107 --> 00:29:57,527
I'm... I'm Maynard.

444
00:29:58,737 --> 00:29:59,821
Maynard.

445
00:30:01,365 --> 00:30:02,950
You two don't know each other?

446
00:30:03,450 --> 00:30:05,076
No, I'm a neighbor.

447
00:30:05,077 --> 00:30:06,161
Friendly neighbor.

448
00:30:09,957 --> 00:30:11,041
Sorry.

449
00:30:11,583 --> 00:30:13,126
So, how was the interview?

450
00:30:13,794 --> 00:30:14,962
I'm gonna go put these in water.

451
00:30:15,462 --> 00:30:17,380
It was nice to meet you, Maynard. Nerd.

452
00:30:17,381 --> 00:30:18,382
Maynard. Yeah.

453
00:30:19,049 --> 00:30:20,800
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

454
00:30:20,801 --> 00:30:23,678
Did you go? Please tell me that you went.

455
00:30:23,679 --> 00:30:24,887
Yeah. No, I went.

456
00:30:24,888 --> 00:30:26,430
And?

457
00:30:26,431 --> 00:30:27,640
And I got the job.

458
00:30:27,641 --> 00:30:29,850
Oh, my God, MJ, that's amazing.

459
00:30:29,851 --> 00:30:31,727
I turned it down.

460
00:30:31,728 --> 00:30:32,979
What?

461
00:30:32,980 --> 00:30:35,274
Yeah. I don't wanna work
for some soulless corporation.

462
00:30:36,316 --> 00:30:38,235
They're not all soulless.

463
00:30:39,194 --> 00:30:41,153
Okay. They're all mostly soulless.

464
00:30:41,154 --> 00:30:43,114
But don't you want, like,
health insurance?

465
00:30:43,115 --> 00:30:45,449
Yeah, of course I do. But at what cost?

466
00:30:45,450 --> 00:30:47,077
Depends on your deductible.

467
00:30:48,578 --> 00:30:49,954
You mean, like, your principles?

468
00:30:49,955 --> 00:30:51,122
- Yes.
- Sorry.

469
00:30:51,123 --> 00:30:52,540
I don't know. I know it sounds cheesy,

470
00:30:52,541 --> 00:30:54,959
but something is just telling me

471
00:30:54,960 --> 00:30:58,463
that I'm supposed to be waiting
for something great, you know?

472
00:30:59,673 --> 00:31:03,593
Okay. Well, to waiting
for something great.

473
00:31:04,219 --> 00:31:05,429
To waiting for something great.

474
00:31:06,013 --> 00:31:07,848
Well, the wait is over.

475
00:31:09,141 --> 00:31:10,308
To your new home.

476
00:31:10,309 --> 00:31:11,726
Dude, this is top-shelf.

477
00:31:11,727 --> 00:31:12,769
Just like you.

478
00:31:14,313 --> 00:31:15,314
Dude.

479
00:31:16,148 --> 00:31:17,149
I'm gonna hide this.

480
00:31:19,568 --> 00:31:20,986
I lifted this off of him again.

481
00:31:22,863 --> 00:31:25,573
But what if Ned needs
the fire of a thousand sharks?

482
00:31:25,574 --> 00:31:26,783
You mean heart palpitations?

483
00:31:28,910 --> 00:31:30,621
- You can't save everyone.
- I can try.

484
00:31:33,165 --> 00:31:34,166
That's my girl.

485
00:31:50,807 --> 00:31:51,850
I'm sorry. I gotta...

486
00:32:12,955 --> 00:32:15,874
When we get into MIT,
we should live together.

487
00:32:16,500 --> 00:32:18,335
<i>- Yeah, for sure.
- Yeah, I'd love that.</i>

488
00:32:18,794 --> 00:32:21,546
Be a fresh start.
And we'll all be together.

489
00:32:23,215 --> 00:32:24,674
Yeah, no, you're right. Yeah.

490
00:32:24,675 --> 00:32:25,801
Fresh start.

491
00:32:28,887 --> 00:32:30,222
<i>You're gonna forget who I am.</i>

492
00:32:31,056 --> 00:32:32,932
<i>Forget who you are?
What are you talking about?</i>

493
00:32:32,933 --> 00:32:37,104
<i>It's okay. I'm gonna come and find you,
and I'll explain everything.</i>

494
00:32:38,397 --> 00:32:39,731
- I love...
- Just wait.

495
00:32:40,899 --> 00:32:42,943
