742
00:53:09,336 --> 00:53:10,879
You better pick up the pace.

743
00:53:17,803 --> 00:53:19,805
E.V., track physical anomalies.

744
00:53:20,973 --> 00:53:24,016
{\an8}<i>Searching for physical anomalies
between subjects.</i>

745
00:53:24,017 --> 00:53:25,060
{\an8}<i>Please stand by.</i>

746
00:53:29,690 --> 00:53:32,109
Thank you all so much for coming today.

747
00:53:39,074 --> 00:53:40,491
I'm sorry about that.

748
00:53:40,492 --> 00:53:42,535
Give it up for Spider-Man,

749
00:53:42,536 --> 00:53:45,789
in a race for the love of his life,
and it's not looking good.

750
00:53:48,041 --> 00:53:50,294
Come on, Spidey. Keep up.

751
00:53:51,378 --> 00:53:52,379
Excuse me. Sorry.

752
00:54:01,263 --> 00:54:02,264
Spider-Man!

753
00:54:05,934 --> 00:54:07,769
E.V., run these numbers with the others.

754
00:54:11,064 --> 00:54:13,400
{\an8}<i>Analyzing jump distances for patterns.</i>

755
00:54:15,777 --> 00:54:17,112
Get me that jump data.

756
00:54:17,529 --> 00:54:18,530
{\an8}<i>Calculating.</i>

757
00:54:22,409 --> 00:54:24,036
Come on, I need an answer!

758
00:54:25,662 --> 00:54:27,247
{\an8}<i>Calculations complete.</i>

759
00:54:42,846 --> 00:54:45,015
You have a limit
to your jump radius, don't ya?

760
00:54:45,599 --> 00:54:46,683
Thirty-three feet.

761
00:54:47,684 --> 00:54:49,936
I don't see anybody up here
for you to hop into.

762
00:54:51,313 --> 00:54:52,439
Very clever.

763
00:54:52,898 --> 00:54:56,068
Like I said, you're not getting near her.

764
00:55:11,792 --> 00:55:13,376
- Hey, hey, hey.
- I'm sorry, but you're in danger.

765
00:55:13,377 --> 00:55:14,460
- Where's your roommate?
- What?

766
00:55:14,461 --> 00:55:15,544
Where's Ned?

767
00:55:15,545 --> 00:55:16,796
In Boston with friends. Why?

768
00:55:16,797 --> 00:55:18,172
Okay, good. You gotta come with me.

769
00:55:18,173 --> 00:55:19,966
What? I don't know
if you're the real Spider-Man.

770
00:55:19,967 --> 00:55:21,550
- I'm not coming with you.
- We don't have time for this.

771
00:55:21,551 --> 00:55:23,803
- Please. Come on.
- You need to get out of my apartment.

772
00:55:23,804 --> 00:55:25,262
Look, this is gonna sound insane,

773
00:55:25,263 --> 00:55:27,848
but there is someone who is after you
who is really dangerous, okay?

774
00:55:27,849 --> 00:55:29,643
And I promised you
that I would keep you safe.

775
00:55:30,769 --> 00:55:32,688
Please, you just have to trust me.
Come on.

776
00:55:36,149 --> 00:55:37,234
Fine.

777
00:55:43,907 --> 00:55:45,075
Web. Stop.

778
00:55:48,578 --> 00:55:49,579
Web. Stop.

779
00:55:53,750 --> 00:55:54,835
Web. Stop.

780
00:56:00,424 --> 00:56:01,882
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, yeah, I'm fine.

781
00:56:01,883 --> 00:56:04,468
Okay. We should be safe up here.

782
00:56:04,469 --> 00:56:05,554
Okay, well, safe from what?

783
00:56:06,930 --> 00:56:08,306
I'm not entirely sure.

784
00:56:08,307 --> 00:56:09,850
Okay, well, what do they want with me?

785
00:56:10,600 --> 00:56:12,269
- I don't know.
- You don't know?

786
00:56:12,811 --> 00:56:15,397
It doesn't make any sense.
Why would they choose me?

787
00:56:16,148 --> 00:56:18,150
I wish I could tell you. I just...

788
00:56:20,861 --> 00:56:22,404
We knew each other, didn't we?

789
00:56:26,074 --> 00:56:27,075
What?

790
00:56:28,076 --> 00:56:29,411
It's the only explanation.

791
00:56:30,746 --> 00:56:32,204
It's been driving me crazy for years,

792
00:56:32,205 --> 00:56:34,541
all the times that Spider-Man
saved either me or Ned.

793
00:56:35,292 --> 00:56:36,459
It was the Washington Monument,

794
00:56:36,460 --> 00:56:39,004
and then it was London and Prague
and the Night Monkey.

795
00:56:39,921 --> 00:56:42,341
I mean, twice is a coincidence,
but over and over again...

796
00:56:44,760 --> 00:56:46,470
We knew each other. Tell me I'm wrong.

797
00:56:48,513 --> 00:56:49,680
Well, you're wrong.

798
00:56:49,681 --> 00:56:52,476
What were we? Were we classmates
or friends or something?

799
00:56:53,060 --> 00:56:55,478
Look, I... I don't know
what you're talking about.

800
00:56:55,479 --> 00:56:56,647
Were we something more?

801
00:56:58,815 --> 00:57:01,151
I just, I can't... I can't remember.

802
00:57:01,276 --> 00:57:03,361
And I feel like
someone scrambled my brain.

803
00:57:03,362 --> 00:57:05,238
And you're the only one
who would know why.

804
00:57:06,323 --> 00:57:07,698
This is crazy. I can't...

805
00:57:07,699 --> 00:57:09,618
I know that you can't
tell me the truth.

806
00:57:12,579 --> 00:57:13,830
But I need to know.

807
00:57:19,002 --> 00:57:21,004
Maybe there's a part of me
that still remembers.

808
00:58:01,628 --> 00:58:02,629
Peter.

809
00:58:04,673 --> 00:58:05,840
MJ.

810
00:58:05,841 --> 00:58:06,925
Hey, Peter.

811
00:58:13,181 --> 00:58:14,891
I've missed you so much.

812
00:58:19,855 --> 00:58:21,565
I can't believe you figured it out.

813
00:58:21,982 --> 00:58:23,025
I did.

814
00:58:28,780 --> 00:58:31,241
Go ahead, Peter. Touch her.

815
00:58:32,659 --> 00:58:33,952
Hold her.

816
00:58:35,329 --> 00:58:36,788
You've been wanting to for so long.

817
00:58:45,672 --> 00:58:47,341
True love's kiss breaks the spell

818
00:58:48,216 --> 00:58:50,052
and reunites the star-crossed lovers.

819
00:58:52,304 --> 00:58:53,472
MJ would vomit.

820
00:58:56,224 --> 00:58:57,851
You really are a simple spider,
aren't you?

821
00:59:01,396 --> 00:59:02,397
I see why you like her.

822
00:59:03,065 --> 00:59:04,107
She's...

823
00:59:05,275 --> 00:59:06,693
she's smart...

824
00:59:07,235 --> 00:59:08,278
funny...

825
00:59:09,154 --> 00:59:10,447
and a little dark and twisted.

826
00:59:14,493 --> 00:59:15,577
I mean, it is sad.

827
00:59:16,703 --> 00:59:19,831
There is, like,
no thoughts of you in here...

828
00:59:21,208 --> 00:59:22,417
whatsoever.

829
00:59:23,961 --> 00:59:25,295
But you knew that, didn't you?

830
00:59:26,672 --> 00:59:27,965
You're a monster.

831
00:59:28,924 --> 00:59:30,800
If you loved someone
the way that I love her,

832
00:59:30,801 --> 00:59:33,678
then you'd know that what you're doing
right now is unforgivable.

833
00:59:33,679 --> 00:59:34,763
Is that so?

834
00:59:41,770 --> 00:59:44,815
You know, some people would kill to hold
the person they love one last time.

835
00:59:46,733 --> 00:59:48,110
Stop it now.

836
00:59:57,911 --> 00:59:59,288
You're running out of time, Peter.

837
01:00:00,455 --> 01:00:03,959
Soon enough, it won't just be your friends
who don't remember Peter Parker.

838
01:00:05,460 --> 01:00:07,170
Maybe you should
write a letter to yourself.

839
01:00:11,800 --> 01:00:12,843
Get out of her.

840
01:00:14,386 --> 01:00:15,762
Who's the monster now, Peter?

841
01:00:39,119 --> 01:00:40,120
MJ.

842
01:00:40,746 --> 01:00:43,164
MJ. No, no, no. Oh, God.

843
01:00:43,165 --> 01:00:44,874
Oh, God, please, no, come on.

844
01:00:44,875 --> 01:00:46,626
Come on, come on, come on.

845
01:00:46,627 --> 01:00:49,253
Oh, thank God. Oh, thank God.

846
01:00:49,254 --> 01:00:52,256
Oh, you're okay. Oh, you're okay.

847
01:00:52,257 --> 01:00:53,508
Oh, I'm so sorry.

848
01:00:55,969 --> 01:00:58,304
Stop. Wait, wait, stop, stop,
please, I'll quit.

849
01:00:58,305 --> 01:01:00,432
You... You win, you win, you win.
Just don't hurt her.

850
01:01:03,477 --> 01:01:04,936
You're a mess, Spider-Man.

851
01:01:07,648 --> 01:01:09,273
Anytime I want...

852
01:01:09,274 --> 01:01:10,609
I can be anyone I want.

853
01:01:11,860 --> 01:01:13,612
So you can't protect MJ,

854
01:01:14,988 --> 01:01:16,615
even from herself.

855
01:01:23,789 --> 01:01:25,457
It really is a nice letter.

856
01:01:26,416 --> 01:01:27,541
Little heavy-handed.

857
01:01:27,542 --> 01:01:28,710
But not bad.

858
01:01:47,688 --> 01:01:50,314
You're okay.
I'm gonna take you someplace safe.

859
01:01:50,315 --> 01:01:51,316
What?

860
01:01:52,734 --> 01:01:54,026
Take me to 3165...

861
01:01:54,027 --> 01:01:55,361
Lafayette Street.

862
01:01:55,362 --> 01:01:57,698
<i>Navigating to Empire State University.</i>

863
01:02:02,744 --> 01:02:04,037
Wait, wait, wait! Okay.

864
01:02:06,081 --> 01:02:07,415
- I got you. I got you.
- Are you sure?

865
01:02:07,416 --> 01:02:08,499
- Yep.
- Okay.

866
01:02:08,500 --> 01:02:09,750
'Cause I feel like
I'm slipping a little bit.

867
01:02:09,751 --> 01:02:10,752
- You're not slipping.
- Okay.

868
01:02:12,629 --> 01:02:13,963
You're okay, you're okay, you're okay.

869
01:02:13,964 --> 01:02:15,632
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'm fine. I'm fine.

870
01:02:18,927 --> 01:02:20,011
Okay.

871
01:02:20,012 --> 01:02:21,387
Can we just slow down

872
01:02:21,388 --> 01:02:22,763
- for like two seconds, please?
- Well, we're almost there.

873
01:02:22,764 --> 01:02:25,182
Yeah, yeah, but you just told me
I was mind controlled.

874
01:02:25,183 --> 01:02:26,267
Well, not technically.

875
01:02:26,268 --> 01:02:27,518
I mean, you're lucky
I believe in that stuff, okay?

876
01:02:27,519 --> 01:02:29,646
Because governments have been doing it
for years, especially the French.

877
01:02:30,355 --> 01:02:31,647
- Are you okay?
- Yeah...

878
01:02:31,648 --> 01:02:34,026
Look. Sorry. I'm just trying
to take you someplace safe, okay?

879
01:02:38,655 --> 01:02:39,906
I don't feel safe.

880
01:02:41,992 --> 01:02:42,993
Oh, shit.

881
01:02:47,998 --> 01:02:49,207
- Sorry.
- Oh, watch out!

882
01:02:58,800 --> 01:03:00,052
You're losing it, kid.

883
01:03:00,427 --> 01:03:03,054
Thought you'd be able to see that coming
a mile away.

884
01:03:03,055 --> 01:03:04,221
What is wrong with you?

885
01:03:04,222 --> 01:03:05,432
- You could've killed us.
- Excuse me.

886
01:03:05,849 --> 01:03:08,476
You show up to my house unannounced,
what do you think's gonna happen?

887
01:03:08,477 --> 01:03:09,602
Wait, this is your house?

888
01:03:09,603 --> 01:03:10,646
- No, no. Don't, don't, don't.
- Who the hell is that?

889
01:03:11,104 --> 01:03:12,105
Who the hell are you?

890
01:03:12,773 --> 01:03:13,774
She's...

891
01:03:14,733 --> 01:03:15,816
You know.

892
01:03:15,817 --> 01:03:17,985
No, I don't know.
That's why I just asked you.

893
01:03:17,986 --> 01:03:20,905
She's in danger, Frank.
Look, I need your help, okay?

894
01:03:20,906 --> 01:03:22,950
- Yeah, looks like it.
- Well, come on. You owe me.

895
01:03:23,492 --> 01:03:24,909
For... Aren't you sick of this story?

896
01:03:24,910 --> 01:03:25,993
Staten Island!

897
01:03:25,994 --> 01:03:27,536
Nah, Staten Island.

898
01:03:27,537 --> 01:03:30,081
What more do you want me to do?
I literally saved your life.

899
01:03:30,082 --> 01:03:31,165
You're out of your mind, kid!

900
01:03:31,166 --> 01:03:32,333
What, I gotta save it twice

901
01:03:32,334 --> 01:03:33,626
- to get a favor out of you?
- That guy couldn't hit me

902
01:03:33,627 --> 01:03:35,795
- with a handful of rice.
- I mean, what does that sound like to you?

903
01:03:35,796 --> 01:03:37,046
- I had him exactly where I want him.
- A drug dealer was gonna shoot a guy...

904
01:03:37,047 --> 01:03:38,506
- I'm seein' him right there.
- ...then I webbed the gun

905
01:03:38,507 --> 01:03:39,632
- out of the drug dealer's hand...
- I know exactly what

906
01:03:39,633 --> 01:03:41,008
- I'm completely up for.
- ...and then kicked that drug dealer...

907
01:03:41,009 --> 01:03:42,218
- Okay, fine, go ahead.
- ...back into a storage container.

908
01:03:42,219 --> 01:03:43,553
- What would you call that?
- What does that sound like to you?

909
01:03:44,888 --> 01:03:45,973
I don't care. I just wanna go home.

910
01:03:46,974 --> 01:03:49,266
That's an excellent idea. Kick rocks.

911
01:03:49,267 --> 01:03:50,434
- Go home.
- No, no, wait, wait.

912
01:03:50,435 --> 01:03:51,937
Frank, Frank, Frank, wait. Please.

913
01:03:53,105 --> 01:03:56,733
I have got to keep her safe, okay?
And I don't have anywhere else to go.

914
01:04:00,696 --> 01:04:01,697
You like chili?

915
01:04:02,948 --> 01:04:03,949
I made chili.

916
01:04:05,742 --> 01:04:06,743
All right. Just...

917
01:04:07,577 --> 01:04:08,786
watch out for the claymores.

918
01:04:08,787 --> 01:04:11,415
Don't wanna pick up pieces of you
for the next two weeks.

919
01:04:12,833 --> 01:04:14,918
Hey, I definitely
would not eat that chili.

920
01:04:16,795 --> 01:04:18,671
So, you telling me that maniac

921
01:04:18,672 --> 01:04:22,091
behind all that tank nonsense
is nothing but a goddamn teenager?

922
01:04:22,092 --> 01:04:23,259
And it's not just the tank,

923
01:04:23,260 --> 01:04:25,928
it's every attack on Damage Control
this past month.

924
01:04:25,929 --> 01:04:27,930
And how does a kid learn
how to drive a tank?

925
01:04:27,931 --> 01:04:29,181
I don't know, Frank.

926
01:04:29,182 --> 01:04:30,808
Beat your ass
all over the street like that.

927
01:04:30,809 --> 01:04:32,185
She did not beat my ass.

928
01:04:33,145 --> 01:04:34,229
This your family?

929
01:04:37,232 --> 01:04:38,942
Would you get the hell away from that?

930
01:04:39,693 --> 01:04:41,986
Look, I got one rule in this house.

931
01:04:41,987 --> 01:04:44,822
You don't touch anything.
You don't move anything.

932
01:04:44,823 --> 01:04:47,784
You sure as shit don't ask me
any goddamn questions about anything.

933
01:04:49,411 --> 01:04:50,412
So, three rules?

934
01:04:53,707 --> 01:04:55,083
I see why you like her.

935
01:04:56,126 --> 01:04:57,461
I'll go put some pants on.

936
01:04:59,004 --> 01:05:00,297
Don't touch the chili.

937
01:05:02,257 --> 01:05:03,258
I like him.

938
01:05:04,092 --> 01:05:05,135
Of course you do.

939
01:05:06,720 --> 01:05:10,265
So I managed to pull this image from
my HUD and run it through the system.

940
01:05:13,435 --> 01:05:14,602
Who is she?

941
01:05:14,603 --> 01:05:17,105
Until a couple months ago, nobody.

942
01:05:17,981 --> 01:05:20,608
She was in and out of foster care,
psych hospitals,

943
01:05:20,609 --> 01:05:22,653
{\an8}and then eventually she ran away
and dropped off the grid.

944
01:05:22,986 --> 01:05:25,112
{\an8}There's hardly any information about her
that hasn't been scrubbed.

945
01:05:25,113 --> 01:05:29,117
But she's classified as a telepath.
And now we have a name.

946
01:05:32,913 --> 01:05:33,914
"Jean Grey."

947
01:05:35,874 --> 01:05:39,669
Yeah. These are the Damage Control sites
that she hasn't hit yet,

948
01:05:39,670 --> 01:05:41,170
so if she surfaces,

949
01:05:41,171 --> 01:05:43,048
then my facial tracking program
will pick her up.

950
01:05:44,174 --> 01:05:45,341
Right.

951
01:05:45,342 --> 01:05:46,718
Oh, yeah? What then?

952
01:05:49,137 --> 01:05:51,931
Well, don't worry about "what then."
Just look after her.

953
01:05:51,932 --> 01:05:53,557
Don't worry about it, huh?

954
01:05:53,558 --> 01:05:55,559
I'm just supposed to sit here
and babysit your girlfriend?

955
01:05:55,560 --> 01:05:57,395
- I don't need to be babysat, so yeah.
- She's not my girlfriend.

956
01:05:57,396 --> 01:05:59,689
All right, all right.
Look, what's the plan, huh?

957
01:05:59,690 --> 01:06:03,317
Just gonna hope that
your facial tracking program works?

958
01:06:03,318 --> 01:06:05,611
And you get yourself killed,
I gotta watch her the rest of my life?

959
01:06:05,612 --> 01:06:07,947
I'm not gonna get killed, Frank.
I can catch her, okay?

960
01:06:07,948 --> 01:06:09,031
I just...

961
01:06:09,032 --> 01:06:11,535
I just have to fix my inhibitor
and then I'll be good to go.

962
01:06:12,119 --> 01:06:13,495
Well, what do you need to do that?

963
01:06:14,913 --> 01:06:18,458
Frank. You do not have
what I need to do that, okay?

964
01:06:20,002 --> 01:06:21,502
You know you've got some mouth on you.

965
01:06:21,503 --> 01:06:23,504
What do you think,
you have an anti-static mat,

966
01:06:23,505 --> 01:06:25,090
a tonal probe, and micro tools?

967
01:06:25,799 --> 01:06:27,175
I got all that shit.

968
01:06:27,759 --> 01:06:28,843
What for?

969
01:06:28,844 --> 01:06:30,387
- Bombs.
- Bingo.

970
01:06:32,848 --> 01:06:33,932
Unbelievable.

971
01:06:45,777 --> 01:06:48,070
Hey, do you think it's safe
to maybe call someone

972
01:06:48,071 --> 01:06:49,698
and let them know I'm okay?

973
01:06:54,202 --> 01:06:55,203
Like your boyfriend?

974
01:06:56,455 --> 01:06:58,707
No. Like my roommate.

975
01:07:02,753 --> 01:07:05,172
I don't think that's such a good idea,
you know, because...

976
01:07:06,298 --> 01:07:07,882
she already knows who he is,

977
01:07:07,883 --> 01:07:09,759
and she can inhabit anyone
she wants, so...

978
01:07:09,760 --> 01:07:10,926
Right. Yeah.

979
01:07:10,927 --> 01:07:12,303
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You're right.

980
01:07:12,304 --> 01:07:14,973
- Sorry.
- No, it's fine. I totally get it.

981
01:07:17,142 --> 01:07:18,393
If I called my boyfriend,

982
01:07:19,353 --> 01:07:21,604
he'd just ask me a bunch of questions
that I couldn't answer,

983
01:07:21,605 --> 01:07:25,107
and then he'd tell me
I was being withholding again.

984
01:07:25,108 --> 01:07:27,109
- Withholding?
- Yep.

985
01:07:27,110 --> 01:07:28,946
Sounds like your boyfriend's
kind of a jerk.

986
01:07:31,782 --> 01:07:32,950
But why'd he think you're withholding?

987
01:07:33,909 --> 01:07:37,788
I don't know. You tell me,
masked vigilante behind the curtain.

988
01:07:40,040 --> 01:07:41,708
Okay, I see your point.

989
01:07:43,710 --> 01:07:44,795
So what about you?

990
01:07:45,420 --> 01:07:46,421
What about me?

991
01:07:47,381 --> 01:07:50,592
Well, do you have a Mrs. Spider-Man?

992
01:07:52,761 --> 01:07:54,471
Do I have a Mrs. Spider-Man?

993
01:07:58,558 --> 01:08:00,143
No. No.

994
01:08:01,269 --> 01:08:04,106
Why not? Because I'm...

995
01:08:05,857 --> 01:08:07,818
I'm too withholding, obviously.

996
01:08:08,777 --> 01:08:09,820
Welcome to the club.

997
01:08:16,868 --> 01:08:17,953
There was someone.

998
01:08:19,288 --> 01:08:20,580
- Really?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

999
01:08:23,667 --> 01:08:24,750
What happened?

1000
01:08:25,502 --> 01:08:26,503
I...

1001
01:08:28,171 --> 01:08:29,589
I had to let her go.

1002
01:08:30,924 --> 01:08:32,009
To keep her safe.

1003
01:08:36,346 --> 01:08:38,348
I'm sorry.
That must have been really hard for you.

1004
01:08:39,766 --> 01:08:41,685
Yeah, it was. Yeah. It is.

1005
01:08:42,852 --> 01:08:43,895
It is really hard.

1006
01:08:48,275 --> 01:08:49,483
Are you okay?

1007
01:08:49,484 --> 01:08:50,650
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, I'm okay. I...

1008
01:08:50,651 --> 01:08:52,110
You know what, I'm just gonna come over.

1009
01:08:52,111 --> 01:08:54,031
Hold on, hold on, hold on,
hold on, hold on.

1010
01:08:55,906 --> 01:08:56,990
What's going on?

1011
01:08:56,991 --> 01:08:58,826
It just keeps overheating on me.

1012
01:08:59,660 --> 01:09:01,370
It's been stumping me for days.

1013
01:09:02,122 --> 01:09:03,289
Before I switched to aerospace,

1014
01:09:03,290 --> 01:09:07,335
I was gonna major in biochemical
engineering, so, do you mind if I...

1015
01:09:07,336 --> 01:09:08,668
Oh, yeah, for sure.

1016
01:09:08,669 --> 01:09:10,213
Here. There you go.

1017
01:09:13,967 --> 01:09:14,968
Wow.

1018
01:09:18,013 --> 01:09:20,139
So, does the device itself...

1019
01:09:20,140 --> 01:09:23,892
I mean, does it generate
any kind of radiation or a magnetic field?

1020
01:09:23,893 --> 01:09:25,312
'Cause that would definitely interfere.

1021
01:09:25,479 --> 01:09:29,523
Yeah, it has a micro magnetic field,
but I accounted for that in the design.

1022
01:09:29,524 --> 01:09:31,484
Okay, well, what about your suit?

1023
01:09:31,485 --> 01:09:34,821
It actually dissipates into the fabric,
which is pretty cool.

1024
01:09:35,781 --> 01:09:36,781
Okay.

1025
01:09:39,825 --> 01:09:40,953
What about those?

1026
01:09:42,079 --> 01:09:43,080
What about what?

1027
01:09:45,665 --> 01:09:48,209
Your goggles, or whatever you call 'em.

1028
01:09:48,834 --> 01:09:52,047
They would create a field.
It would be tiny, but...

1029
01:09:53,632 --> 01:09:56,050
But it's on your head,
which is very close to the inhibitor.

1030
01:09:56,051 --> 01:09:58,386
Which is probably why it's overheating.

1031
01:09:58,387 --> 01:10:00,222
MJ, that is genius.

1032
01:10:02,015 --> 01:10:03,266
Okay, this has to work.

1033
01:10:07,396 --> 01:10:08,814
<i>Inhibitor engaged.</i>

1034
01:10:10,482 --> 01:10:13,235
{\an8}<i>Suppressing selected arachnid hormones.</i>

1035
01:10:14,194 --> 01:10:16,279
Okay. That feels better.

1036
01:10:16,280 --> 01:10:18,155
That feels totally better.

1037
01:10:18,156 --> 01:10:19,908
My head feels so clear.

1038
01:10:20,951 --> 01:10:22,285
Web, web.

1039
01:10:22,286 --> 01:10:24,453
And I'm not shooting organic webs.

1040
01:10:24,454 --> 01:10:26,707
Oh, my God, MJ,
that, like, totally worked.

1041
01:10:27,749 --> 01:10:30,252
You know, this is some really
intense stuff you're working on here.

1042
01:10:33,088 --> 01:10:34,756
Well, yeah, it's really important.

1043
01:10:37,217 --> 01:10:40,887
Yeah, but this is like, I mean,
this is like altering your DNA.

1044
01:10:42,139 --> 01:10:43,889
I mean, this is the kind of stuff
you put on, like,

1045
01:10:43,890 --> 01:10:45,600
I don't know, like a monster.

1046
01:10:47,853 --> 01:10:51,063
Well, if you've seen what's been happening
to me over the last couple days,

1047
01:10:51,064 --> 01:10:52,316
then you might understand.

1048
01:10:53,025 --> 01:10:54,525
Yeah, well, I've been with you
for the last few hours

1049
01:10:54,526 --> 01:10:55,652
and that's not what I've seen.

1050
01:10:56,486 --> 01:10:57,529
And what have you seen?

1051
01:10:58,822 --> 01:10:59,990
From my side of the curtain?

1052
01:11:02,075 --> 01:11:05,495
A really good guy
who might just be changing.

1053
01:11:10,709 --> 01:11:14,421
Well, I don't mean to overstep.
I'll let you get back to it.

1054
01:11:35,734 --> 01:11:37,027
Can't sleep either, huh?

1055
01:11:37,819 --> 01:11:38,820
You want coffee?

1056
01:11:39,696 --> 01:11:40,739
Sure.

1057
01:11:41,949 --> 01:11:43,158
You get your shit fixed?

1058
01:11:44,117 --> 01:11:46,911
Yeah. I've been wearing it all night.

1059
01:11:46,912 --> 01:11:47,996
So far, so good.

1060
01:11:48,914 --> 01:11:50,748
I made this other one universal.

1061
01:11:50,749 --> 01:11:55,212
So if I could get it on Jean,
it should completely shut down her powers.

1062
01:11:56,171 --> 01:11:57,464
You know what else would work?

1063
01:11:57,839 --> 01:11:59,256
You just shoot her.

1064
01:11:59,257 --> 01:12:00,384
Nice.

1065
01:12:03,136 --> 01:12:04,304
Jesus Christ.

1066
01:12:05,722 --> 01:12:08,099
That has gotta be the goofiest shit
I ever seen in my life.

1067
01:12:08,100 --> 01:12:11,144
What, you can't even take the mask off
to drink a cup of coffee?

1068
01:12:12,396 --> 01:12:15,399
Don't take it personally, Frank.
It stays on for everybody.

1069
01:12:16,441 --> 01:12:17,484
Even her?

1070
01:12:19,945 --> 01:12:21,153
Who is she, kid?

1071
01:12:21,154 --> 01:12:22,238
I don't know.

1072
01:12:22,239 --> 01:12:24,365
That's horseshit. Who is she?

1073
01:12:24,366 --> 01:12:26,826
- I'm telling you, I don't know who she is.
- What are you doin'? You care about her.

1074
01:12:26,827 --> 01:12:28,119
- You're pretending not to. Why?
- I don't care about her.

1075
01:12:28,120 --> 01:12:30,037
Look, I don't know
who she is, Frank. Okay?

1076
01:12:30,038 --> 01:12:32,873
I don't have anybody. I'm like you.
I just keep to myself.

1077
01:12:32,874 --> 01:12:33,917
You're like me?

1078
01:12:35,252 --> 01:12:36,586
What do you know about me, kid?

1079
01:12:37,587 --> 01:12:38,921
You think this is a choice?

1080
01:12:38,922 --> 01:12:41,550
Living like this, it's a lifestyle?
Is that what you think?

1081
01:12:42,217 --> 01:12:43,719
Kid, this is a sentence.

1082
01:12:44,886 --> 01:12:45,887
You know somethin'...

1083
01:12:46,680 --> 01:12:48,098
If I had one second,

1084
01:12:49,057 --> 01:12:52,227
people I love were still breathing,
you think I'd be hiding behind a mask?

1085
01:12:52,853 --> 01:12:55,104
You think I'd pretend
to be something that I'm not,

1086
01:12:55,105 --> 01:12:56,857
acting like a goddamn coward?

1087
01:13:02,487 --> 01:13:03,822
I got a facial match.

1088
01:13:07,993 --> 01:13:10,286
She's at the Damage Control HQ
in Manhattan.

1089
01:13:10,287 --> 01:13:11,496
I gotta go. Okay.

1090
01:13:16,001 --> 01:13:18,085
She's gonna be okay.

1091
01:13:18,086 --> 01:13:19,212
I'll see to it.

1092
01:13:22,257 --> 01:13:23,383
Thanks, Frank.

1093
01:13:30,140 --> 01:13:31,141
Hey.

1094
01:13:31,725 --> 01:13:32,726
Hey.

1095
01:13:34,394 --> 01:13:35,979
You just gonna let him go by himself?

1096
01:13:37,481 --> 01:13:38,857
You know, I think he might need you.

1097
01:13:41,777 --> 01:13:43,445
Kinda like you needed him
on Staten Island.

1098
01:13:47,407 --> 01:13:48,533
Yeah.

1099
01:14:25,862 --> 01:14:27,823
You can't hide from me forever, Bill.

1100
01:14:28,532 --> 01:14:31,785
<i>You've got a strong door,
but it's the wall you have to worry about.</i>

1101
01:14:32,786 --> 01:14:34,329
Who are you and what do you want?

1102
01:14:39,543 --> 01:14:40,794
I'm Jean Grey...

1103
01:14:41,878 --> 01:14:43,463
and you know what I want.

1104
01:15:44,149 --> 01:15:45,359
Jean?

1105
01:15:45,943 --> 01:15:48,612
You looked me up? I'm blushing.

1106
01:15:49,863 --> 01:15:52,240
I told you what would happen to your girl
if you got in my way.

1107
01:15:53,200 --> 01:15:54,868
You're not getting near her again.

1108
01:15:55,410 --> 01:15:57,496
And you're definitely
not getting inside that vault.

1109
01:15:58,038 --> 01:15:59,206
Maybe not.

1110
01:16:06,505 --> 01:16:07,756
But this guy might.

1111
01:16:10,634 --> 01:16:13,386
Jean, you don't know
what you're dealing with.

1112
01:16:13,387 --> 01:16:16,222
You know, you and Banner
have a lot in common.

1113
01:16:16,223 --> 01:16:20,810
Both fighting a losing battle
against the monster that lives inside you.

1114
01:16:20,811 --> 01:16:22,688
Jean, this is the Hulk, you can't just...

1115
01:16:31,280 --> 01:16:32,322
What the hell?

1116
01:16:34,533 --> 01:16:35,659
I see.

1117
01:16:37,577 --> 01:16:41,038
Trying to muzzle me
like you muzzle yourself?

1118
01:16:41,039 --> 01:16:42,623
I can't let you in there.

1119
01:16:42,624 --> 01:16:44,751
Whatever V-Max is, you're not getting it.

1120
01:16:45,210 --> 01:16:46,670
Like hell I'm not.

1121
01:16:47,254 --> 01:16:48,255
Oh, crap.

1122
01:17:00,434 --> 01:17:02,352
Jean, don't do this.

1123
01:17:02,936 --> 01:17:03,937
Save your breath.

1124
01:17:29,379 --> 01:17:31,297
Frank, what are you doing here?

1125
01:17:31,298 --> 01:17:32,965
What you think I'm doing?
I'm saving your ass.

1126
01:17:32,966 --> 01:17:35,092
This is way above your pay grade, dude.

1127
01:17:35,093 --> 01:17:36,428
- We're fighting the Hulk.
- Oh, shit!

1128
01:17:59,159 --> 01:18:00,160
Really?

1129
01:18:12,255 --> 01:18:13,465
Get out!

1130
01:18:19,805 --> 01:18:22,390
- Stop shooting him!
- Are you out of your goddamn mind?

1131
01:18:22,391 --> 01:18:24,643
He's... Banner's not the problem! She is.

1132
01:18:38,323 --> 01:18:40,116
I thought I told you to stay home
and watch MJ.

1133
01:18:40,117 --> 01:18:41,284
Yeah, you did.

1134
01:18:41,285 --> 01:18:43,203
And then she tells me
I gotta come watch you.

1135
01:18:44,496 --> 01:18:46,039
Wait, did she actually say that to you?

1136
01:18:47,040 --> 01:18:48,292
Are you blushing, daffodil?

1137
01:18:49,167 --> 01:18:50,294
I'm not blushing.

1138
01:18:52,254 --> 01:18:55,047
Goddamn it.
I knew I should have brought a bigger gun.

1139
01:18:55,048 --> 01:18:56,340
That's a good idea, "Bring a bigger gun."

1140
01:18:56,341 --> 01:18:57,591
What are you gonna do,
tickle him to death?

1141
01:18:57,592 --> 01:18:59,010
No. Look, change of plan.

1142
01:18:59,011 --> 01:19:01,804
First, we get this on the Hulk,
then we go after Jean.

1143
01:19:01,805 --> 01:19:03,055
I got one better.

1144
01:19:03,056 --> 01:19:05,016
That's the highest
casualty-producing threat.

1145
01:19:05,017 --> 01:19:08,270
You contain it. I go find the source.
I take it down. You got it?

1146
01:19:08,854 --> 01:19:10,731
Are you just trying
to get out of fighting the Hulk?

1147
01:19:12,357 --> 01:19:13,941
- I guess so.
- Okay, whatever, dude.

1148
01:19:13,942 --> 01:19:14,943
I got this.

1149
01:19:15,527 --> 01:19:16,945
- Wait, no, Frank, Frank, Frank.
- What?

1150
01:19:17,321 --> 01:19:18,654
Do not kill her!

1151
01:19:18,655 --> 01:19:20,906
Don't start with that soft serve bullshit.

1152
01:19:20,907 --> 01:19:22,825
You know something?
I'm gonna do this, I'm gonna do it my way.

1153
01:19:22,826 --> 01:19:25,286
Just... just go, just go.

1154
01:19:25,287 --> 01:19:26,830
And don't get within 33 feet!

1155
01:19:27,581 --> 01:19:28,832
So frustrating.

1156
01:19:43,805 --> 01:19:44,806
Hey.

1157
01:19:50,687 --> 01:19:52,856
This guy's got issues.

1158
01:19:54,232 --> 01:19:57,234
No. Oh, no.

1159
01:19:57,235 --> 01:19:59,947
No, not again. Oh, no.

1160
01:20:00,739 --> 01:20:03,283
Dr. Banner? Is that you?

1161
01:20:04,201 --> 01:20:06,535
Spider-Man. What happened?

1162
01:20:06,536 --> 01:20:07,662
Where am I?

1163
01:20:07,663 --> 01:20:09,580
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Did I do all this?

1164
01:20:09,581 --> 01:20:11,082
- You...
- Did I hurt anyone?

1165
01:20:11,083 --> 01:20:13,668
It's not your fault. She was in your mind.
You weren't in control.

1166
01:20:13,669 --> 01:20:15,711
- I lost my inhibitor.
- Look here, here.

1167
01:20:15,712 --> 01:20:18,047
It's the only thing
keeping the monster inside.

1168
01:20:18,048 --> 01:20:19,966
It's okay. I got another one here.
I just need you to put this on.

1169
01:20:19,967 --> 01:20:21,759
- What is it?
- It's universal.

1170
01:20:21,760 --> 01:20:23,053
It should work on you.

1171
01:20:32,437 --> 01:20:34,856
Please, sir, there's people
in the building. Just put it on.

1172
01:20:38,610 --> 01:20:39,777
You okay?

1173
01:20:39,778 --> 01:20:43,114
My head. I think she broke something!

1174
01:20:43,115 --> 01:20:44,407
Is she still in there?

1175
01:20:44,408 --> 01:20:45,741
No.

1176
01:20:45,742 --> 01:20:46,993
It's the other guy.

1177
01:20:46,994 --> 01:20:50,162
Bruce? Look, I can get you
out of here, okay?

1178
01:20:50,163 --> 01:20:51,706
I just need you
to put that inhibitor on.

1179
01:20:51,707 --> 01:20:52,874
Get away from me!

1180
01:20:54,710 --> 01:20:56,044
He's coming.

1181
01:20:56,712 --> 01:20:58,046
I can't control.

1182
01:20:58,755 --> 01:21:00,673
Yes, you can, Bruce! Yes, you can!

1183
01:21:00,674 --> 01:21:04,176
Get out of the building!

1184
01:21:04,177 --> 01:21:05,637
Get everyone out of the...

1185
01:21:09,516 --> 01:21:11,434
No! No!

1186
01:21:11,435 --> 01:21:13,103
Banner, please. Look at me.

1187
01:21:15,772 --> 01:21:18,609
No Banner. No girl.

1188
01:21:19,943 --> 01:21:21,695
Only Hulk.

1189
01:21:31,538 --> 01:21:33,248
I didn't know you could get that big.

1190
01:21:39,338 --> 01:21:40,631
Good luck with that, Peter.

1191
01:21:49,765 --> 01:21:50,766
There you are.

1192
01:21:52,434 --> 01:21:53,435
Just hold still. Just hold still...

1193
01:21:57,022 --> 01:21:58,023
Stay!

1194
01:22:07,282 --> 01:22:08,283
Oh, God.

1195
01:22:23,048 --> 01:22:24,049
No lethal rounds.

1196
01:22:37,062 --> 01:22:38,814
<i>Tracking time to detonation.</i>

1197
01:23:07,759 --> 01:23:09,677
<i>Ninety seconds to detonation.</i>

1198
01:23:09,678 --> 01:23:10,679
I know! I know!

1199
01:23:16,310 --> 01:23:17,768
{\an8}Come on. Come on.

1200
01:23:17,769 --> 01:23:19,395
{\an8}Why is your skin so thick?

1201
01:23:19,396 --> 01:23:20,646
{\an8}<i>Inhibitor cannot attach.</i>

1202
01:23:20,647 --> 01:23:21,773
Come on!

1203
01:24:00,646 --> 01:24:01,647
Dr. Banner...

1204
01:24:03,023 --> 01:24:04,149
please.

1205
01:24:05,609 --> 01:24:06,610
Bruce.

1206
01:24:07,945 --> 01:24:08,946
It's Peter.

1207
01:24:10,656 --> 01:24:12,324
I'm your friend.

1208
01:24:41,645 --> 01:24:42,646
Bruce.

1209
01:25:01,748 --> 01:25:04,543
Throw down your guns,
or you'll get the next one in the head.

1210
01:25:15,846 --> 01:25:17,306
Where is she?

1211
01:25:30,736 --> 01:25:31,819
What did you...

1212
01:25:31,820 --> 01:25:33,030
It's over, Jean.

1213
01:25:48,378 --> 01:25:49,379
Sara.

1214
01:26:00,682 --> 01:26:01,808
Is that my gun?

1215
01:26:10,817 --> 01:26:13,528
Is anyone hurt? It's just me?

1216
01:26:14,488 --> 01:26:15,697
Is anyone hurt?

1217
01:26:17,324 --> 01:26:18,325
Spider-Man...

1218
01:26:21,078 --> 01:26:22,162
You saved my life.

1219
01:26:23,080 --> 01:26:24,747
And you saved God knows how many lives

1220
01:26:24,748 --> 01:26:27,500
by making sure she didn't find
what she was looking for in there.

1221
01:26:27,501 --> 01:26:28,835
Still inside. We got her coming through.

1222
01:26:29,962 --> 01:26:31,838
Before she passed out,
she tried to say something.

1223
01:26:32,965 --> 01:26:35,634
A name, Sara.
Does that mean something to you?

1224
01:26:36,969 --> 01:26:38,720
Before you got the inhibitor on her,

1225
01:26:39,805 --> 01:26:41,807
she managed to get in my mind
for a moment.

1226
01:26:43,350 --> 01:26:46,812
Sara was the name of someone I worked
closely with that recently passed.

1227
01:26:47,437 --> 01:26:48,522
I'm sorry to hear that.

1228
01:26:50,023 --> 01:26:53,819
Somehow the memory of Sara
must have affected her.

1229
01:26:56,822 --> 01:26:59,740
Well, I'd love to talk to her
when she wakes up, if that's all right.

1230
01:26:59,741 --> 01:27:03,786
Of course. She'll be transferred
to our facility on Roosevelt Island.

1231
01:27:03,787 --> 01:27:06,205
Now, I'm just as eager
to get her talking as you are,

1232
01:27:06,206 --> 01:27:08,125
but let's not strain her
too much in one day.

1233
01:27:08,750 --> 01:27:09,835
Yeah, of course.

1234
01:27:10,585 --> 01:27:12,003
Thank you, Spider-Man.

1235
01:27:12,004 --> 01:27:13,005
My pleasure.

1236
01:27:24,933 --> 01:27:26,017
MJ!

1237
01:27:26,018 --> 01:27:28,394
It worked. She's in custody.

1238
01:27:28,395 --> 01:27:29,563
You're safe now.

1239
01:27:32,691 --> 01:27:33,692
You left this.

1240
01:27:41,992 --> 01:27:43,243
Did you want me to find it?

1241
01:27:45,370 --> 01:27:47,247
No. No.

1242
01:27:48,457 --> 01:27:49,540
Look, I can explain, I...

1243
01:27:49,541 --> 01:27:50,959
Can you take that off, please?

1244
01:27:52,836 --> 01:27:53,837
What?

1245
01:27:54,880 --> 01:27:55,881
The mask.

1246
01:27:57,966 --> 01:28:02,554
I think I deserve to have
this conversation with "Peter Parker."

1247
01:28:28,538 --> 01:28:30,415
You came to the party
at our apartment the other night.

1248
01:28:36,964 --> 01:28:38,131
And the donut shop.

1249
01:28:40,384 --> 01:28:41,718
The year I went off to school.

1250
01:28:44,596 --> 01:28:45,722
Why didn't you tell me then?

1251
01:28:46,473 --> 01:28:48,058
I was trying to protect you.

1252
01:28:48,600 --> 01:28:51,519
Yeah, well, I've almost been killed, like,
five times in the past 24 hours,

1253
01:28:51,520 --> 01:28:53,063
so it's not really working that well.

1254
01:28:53,939 --> 01:28:55,274
I know. I'm sorry. I...

1255
01:28:56,692 --> 01:28:57,985
Were you ever gonna tell me?

1256
01:29:04,908 --> 01:29:05,909
Right.

1257
01:29:07,411 --> 01:29:09,830
So you just were gonna
make that decision for me.

1258
01:29:10,580 --> 01:29:11,789
I know. I'm sorry.

1259
01:29:11,790 --> 01:29:13,749
I don't really need you to keep saying
that you're sorry.

1260
01:29:13,750 --> 01:29:15,042
I don't know
what you want me to tell you.

1261
01:29:15,043 --> 01:29:16,920
I want you to tell me
why you would do this to me.

1262
01:29:23,051 --> 01:29:24,303
I lost someone.

1263
01:29:28,265 --> 01:29:30,392
And they'd still be here
if it wasn't for me.

1264
01:29:35,188 --> 01:29:36,815
I didn't read you that letter because...

1265
01:29:38,108 --> 01:29:40,526
I didn't want anything like that
to happen to you.

1266
01:29:40,527 --> 01:29:41,819
But that's not really
your decision to make.

1267
01:29:41,820 --> 01:29:43,113
I know it's not, but...

1268
01:29:45,490 --> 01:29:46,825
You mean everything to me.

1269
01:29:50,078 --> 01:29:52,497
And I've been trying to live my life
without you, but I...

1270
01:29:54,374 --> 01:29:55,375
I can't.

1271
01:30:01,590 --> 01:30:02,591
I love you.

1272
01:30:14,686 --> 01:30:17,773
This spell or whatever it is
that you did...

1273
01:30:21,443 --> 01:30:22,444
It worked.

1274
01:30:25,405 --> 01:30:28,659
All these memories that you're saying
that we have together, I don't...

1275
01:30:30,911 --> 01:30:32,037
I don't have them.

1276
01:30:35,832 --> 01:30:38,084
And I do see why, you know,
she would love you,

1277
01:30:38,085 --> 01:30:40,796
the girl you wrote that letter to, but...

1278
01:30:45,550 --> 01:30:46,635
I understand...

1279
01:30:47,678 --> 01:30:50,597
that you did what you had to do
to protect her.

1280
01:30:52,891 --> 01:30:55,602
And for that I'm so grateful.

1281
01:30:59,106 --> 01:31:00,107
But I...

1282
01:31:04,152 --> 01:31:05,445
I don't love you.

1283
01:31:09,825 --> 01:31:10,826
Because I don't...

1284
01:31:11,451 --> 01:31:13,036
I don't even know you.

1285
01:31:21,753 --> 01:31:24,131
I should probably go now.

1286
01:31:30,554 --> 01:31:32,055
I really am sorry, Peter.

1287
01:31:50,407 --> 01:31:51,617
I don't have a phone.

1288
01:31:54,828 --> 01:31:56,163
Do you mind taking me home?

1289
01:31:58,999 --> 01:32:00,166
Yeah, of course.

1290
01:32:00,167 --> 01:32:01,168
Thank you.

1291
01:32:44,044 --> 01:32:45,629
- Thank you.
- Yeah, sure.

1292
01:32:46,838 --> 01:32:48,047
I'm going to...

1293
01:32:48,048 --> 01:32:49,549
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, of course.

1294
01:32:59,059 --> 01:33:00,143
Do you wanna come up?

1295
01:33:02,312 --> 01:33:04,564
Just to say hi to Ned. Maybe.

1296
01:33:07,985 --> 01:33:08,986
I would love that.

1297
01:33:09,945 --> 01:33:11,028
Okay.

1298
01:33:11,029 --> 01:33:14,365
<i>The Hulk, a.k.a. Dr. Bruce Banner,
is in custody,</i>

1299
01:33:14,366 --> 01:33:16,742
<i>currently being transferred
to a psychiatric ward.</i>

1300
01:33:16,743 --> 01:33:17,952
So sad.

1301
01:33:17,953 --> 01:33:20,329
<i>After years as a peaceful academic,</i>

1302
01:33:20,330 --> 01:33:23,249
<i>the question the world asked today is,</i>

1303
01:33:23,250 --> 01:33:24,710
<i>"What finally snapped?"</i>

1304
01:33:31,008 --> 01:33:32,592
<i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1305
01:33:32,926 --> 01:33:34,677
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
- MJ?

1306
01:33:34,678 --> 01:33:36,221
- Yeah.
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1307
01:33:37,139 --> 01:33:38,472
<i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1308
01:33:38,473 --> 01:33:39,682
You're not gonna believe this...

1309
01:33:39,683 --> 01:33:41,684
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
- ...but the Spidey Tracker app

1310
01:33:41,685 --> 01:33:42,893
- says that Spider-Man...
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1311
01:33:42,894 --> 01:33:45,104
- ...is in the direct vicinity.
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1312
01:33:45,105 --> 01:33:46,773
- Oh, yeah? No way. That's crazy.
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1313
01:33:47,482 --> 01:33:48,859
<i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1314
01:33:50,110 --> 01:33:52,029
Ned, Spider-Man. Spider-Man, Ned.

1315
01:33:52,487 --> 01:33:53,654
It's nice to meet you, Ned.

1316
01:33:53,655 --> 01:33:54,823
Hello.

1317
01:33:55,532 --> 01:33:56,616
I'm not, like, a weirdo

1318
01:33:56,617 --> 01:33:57,701
- or anything, I'm...
- He's a little weird.

1319
01:33:58,201 --> 01:34:00,370
Why... Why are you here?

1320
01:34:01,413 --> 01:34:02,705
- I...
- I was...

1321
01:34:02,706 --> 01:34:04,957
- I was on a subway platform.
- She was in the... Platform. Right.

1322
01:34:04,958 --> 01:34:06,042
- And she was on her phone.
- Yeah, and...

1323
01:34:06,043 --> 01:34:07,126
Yeah, I got a little distracted.

1324
01:34:07,127 --> 01:34:08,336
- And the train was coming and he...
- I mean...

1325
01:34:08,337 --> 01:34:09,629
And I just swooped her right up.

1326
01:34:09,630 --> 01:34:11,131
- Yep. Saved me.
- Yeah.

1327
01:34:12,841 --> 01:34:14,426
Oh, my God.

1328
01:34:15,510 --> 01:34:16,970
Why has that never happened to me?

1329
01:34:17,512 --> 01:34:21,057
So what if you're mid-swing
and you decide you need to pee?

1330
01:34:21,058 --> 01:34:22,683
Do you just land on top of a building?

1331
01:34:22,684 --> 01:34:23,893
What?

1332
01:34:23,894 --> 01:34:24,977
Do you drop down to ground level

1333
01:34:24,978 --> 01:34:26,187
and run into a coffee shop
and you're like,

1334
01:34:26,188 --> 01:34:27,521
"Hey, it's Spider-Man. I need to pee"?

1335
01:34:27,522 --> 01:34:29,357
Or do you find a rooftop somewhere?

1336
01:34:29,358 --> 01:34:31,275
No, I don't find a rooftop somewhere, Ned.

1337
01:34:31,276 --> 01:34:33,361
Is this really
what you wanna be asking him right now?

1338
01:34:33,362 --> 01:34:34,946
Yeah, dude, come on,
you can ask me anything.

1339
01:34:34,947 --> 01:34:36,530
You wanna know how my web shooters work?

1340
01:34:36,531 --> 01:34:38,157
I mean, I already know
how the web shooters work.

1341
01:34:38,158 --> 01:34:39,492
Is that right?

1342
01:34:39,493 --> 01:34:42,662
Well, there's obviously
some sort of a shear-thinning fluid

1343
01:34:42,663 --> 01:34:46,248
that is cycling within a chamber, right?
So it can keep its liquid form.

1344
01:34:46,249 --> 01:34:48,668
And then, when you activate it
by pressing on the triggers,

1345
01:34:48,669 --> 01:34:50,336
it runs through a Teflon turbine,

1346
01:34:50,337 --> 01:34:54,132
and then it hardens
when it interacts with the air. Right?

1347
01:34:57,177 --> 01:34:59,303
I mean, not exactly, but...

1348
01:34:59,304 --> 01:35:01,681
Okay, okay, well, then tell me
what's in the web fluid.

1349
01:35:01,682 --> 01:35:04,934
I would guess something
like a long chain polymer.

1350
01:35:04,935 --> 01:35:06,102
Nylon?

1351
01:35:06,103 --> 01:35:07,186
That's pretty close.

1352
01:35:07,187 --> 01:35:10,148
Okay, okay. What about Nomex or Kevlar?

1353
01:35:12,734 --> 01:35:14,652
"All right, then. Keep your secrets."

1354
01:35:14,653 --> 01:35:17,863
"If you're referring
to the incident with the dragon,

1355
01:35:17,864 --> 01:35:19,198
"I was barely involved."

1356
01:35:19,199 --> 01:35:22,911
"All I did was simply give your uncle
a little nudge out the door."

1357
01:35:25,455 --> 01:35:26,540
Solid reference.

1358
01:35:28,250 --> 01:35:29,542
Banh mi time.

1359
01:35:29,543 --> 01:35:31,002
You ordered banh mis?

1360
01:35:31,003 --> 01:35:32,295
I ordered five banh mis.

1361
01:35:32,296 --> 01:35:34,214
We have Spider-Man in the apartment.
He's gonna get fed.

1362
01:35:37,884 --> 01:35:40,970
Sorry about him. He's just, like,
very excited that you're here.

1363
01:35:40,971 --> 01:35:43,307
You kidding? This is, like,
the most fun I've had in years.

1364
01:35:43,974 --> 01:35:45,475
I really missed you guys.

1365
01:35:47,394 --> 01:35:49,478
You guys really do look like best friends.

1366
01:35:49,479 --> 01:35:50,480
What do you mean?

1367
01:36:00,032 --> 01:36:01,033
You should tell him.

1368
01:36:01,783 --> 01:36:02,784
He can handle it.

1369
01:36:04,661 --> 01:36:05,662
Yeah, I know.

1370
01:36:12,794 --> 01:36:16,131
When she was inhabiting you
on the rooftop,

1371
01:36:17,549 --> 01:36:18,759
she kissed me...

1372
01:36:19,801 --> 01:36:21,510
and I kissed her back,

1373
01:36:21,511 --> 01:36:23,972
because I... I thought it was you,
but I didn't know.

1374
01:36:24,723 --> 01:36:26,516
And I'm... I'm really sorry.

1375
01:36:27,893 --> 01:36:29,186
I just thought you should know.

1376
01:36:31,605 --> 01:36:32,606
Thanks for telling me.

1377
01:36:36,234 --> 01:36:38,987
I mean, it's not like
I remember anything anyway, so...

1378
01:36:40,405 --> 01:36:41,572
Really?

1379
01:36:41,573 --> 01:36:44,492
Yeah. It was weird, it was like,
one second I was sitting at my desk,

1380
01:36:44,493 --> 01:36:46,244
and the next second
I was lying on the street.

1381
01:36:47,162 --> 01:36:48,705
I don't know,
like a light switch went off.

1382
01:36:51,249 --> 01:36:52,416
What?

1383
01:36:52,417 --> 01:36:53,794
So you don't remember anything?

1384
01:36:55,837 --> 01:36:56,921
No. Why?

1385
01:36:56,922 --> 01:36:59,966
Metzger said he remembered
thinking about someone named Sara,

1386
01:36:59,967 --> 01:37:03,220
but what you're saying is that
you don't remember anything at all?

1387
01:37:05,347 --> 01:37:07,807
I mean, yeah, it was instantaneous.

1388
01:37:07,808 --> 01:37:08,976
That's what made it so scary.

1389
01:37:11,019 --> 01:37:12,270
He lied to me.

1390
01:37:15,315 --> 01:37:16,941
<i>I heard you caught leshy.</i>

1391
01:37:16,942 --> 01:37:18,317
Yeah. Her name's Jean Grey.

1392
01:37:18,318 --> 01:37:20,778
I need some help
determining the size of some potatoes.

1393
01:37:20,779 --> 01:37:22,655
- Potatoes?
- I think that's Black Widow.

1394
01:37:22,656 --> 01:37:24,699
I think Metzger lied to me about a name.

1395
01:37:24,700 --> 01:37:28,245
<i>Can you see if there's a connection
between Jean and someone named Sara?</i>

1396
01:37:29,371 --> 01:37:31,039
These potatoes sound meager.

1397
01:37:32,708 --> 01:37:34,459
Wow. That really is your office.

1398
01:37:35,168 --> 01:37:36,335
Well, well, well.

1399
01:37:36,336 --> 01:37:38,796
Internet, government records,

1400
01:37:38,797 --> 01:37:43,592
and a lot of data related to Jean Grey
has been scrubbed by Damage Control.

1401
01:37:43,593 --> 01:37:44,594
<i>Data about what?</i>

1402
01:37:45,554 --> 01:37:46,555
Her sister.

1403
01:37:47,264 --> 01:37:48,682
Wait, Jean has a sister?

1404
01:37:51,268 --> 01:37:52,351
Sara Grey.

1405
01:37:52,352 --> 01:37:54,145
<i>Also a telepath.</i>

1406
01:37:54,146 --> 01:37:58,024
<i>Damage Control took her into custody
for study and observation.</i>

1407
01:37:58,025 --> 01:38:00,359
<i>Wow. I mean, you can probably guess
what they mean by that.</i>

1408
01:38:00,360 --> 01:38:02,737
Experimentation
and other human rights violations.

1409
01:38:02,738 --> 01:38:04,614
Yes, exactly. Wait, who are you?

1410
01:38:04,615 --> 01:38:06,449
<i>- Hi. Ned Leeds. Big fan.
- I'm...</i>

1411
01:38:06,450 --> 01:38:07,825
Hi.

1412
01:38:07,826 --> 01:38:08,910
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

1413
01:38:09,369 --> 01:38:12,372
I'm just so happy
that the sad man has friends.

1414
01:38:14,541 --> 01:38:16,752
Thanks. I owe you one.

1415
01:38:17,878 --> 01:38:19,253
<i>Good luck, Spider-Man.</i>

1416
01:38:19,254 --> 01:38:20,379
Bye.

1417
01:38:20,380 --> 01:38:21,922
She was just looking for her sister

1418
01:38:21,923 --> 01:38:24,133
and I handed her
to the people that took her.

1419
01:38:24,134 --> 01:38:25,801
- I gotta go.
- Hey, Peter...

1420
01:38:25,802 --> 01:38:26,803
Yeah?

1421
01:38:27,846 --> 01:38:28,930
Just be careful, all right?

1422
01:38:30,807 --> 01:38:31,808
Yeah, I will.

1423
01:38:36,647 --> 01:38:38,315
Spider-Man's name is Peter?

1424
01:38:51,995 --> 01:38:54,289
Jean, who do you want to be?

1425
01:38:56,833 --> 01:38:58,210
Her. Pink jacket.

1426
01:38:59,836 --> 01:39:00,837
She's too far.

1427
01:39:01,880 --> 01:39:02,964
You're gonna have to hop.

1428
01:39:02,965 --> 01:39:04,423
Hop?

1429
01:39:04,424 --> 01:39:06,468
First, pick someone close.

1430
01:39:07,135 --> 01:39:08,136
And then...

1431
01:39:22,317 --> 01:39:23,318
Each hop has a limit.

1432
01:39:23,986 --> 01:39:27,197
But you can string them together
and go as far as you want.

1433
01:39:27,864 --> 01:39:29,116
And when you let go...

1434
01:39:30,409 --> 01:39:31,702
You're right back where you started.

1435
01:39:32,911 --> 01:39:35,163
Could you do that
to everyone in this park at once?

1436
01:39:36,123 --> 01:39:37,457
Well, yeah, maybe one day.

1437
01:39:38,166 --> 01:39:39,376
If you get really good.

1438
01:39:53,015 --> 01:39:54,016
How could she just...

1439
01:39:55,267 --> 01:39:56,310
send us away?

1440
01:39:57,936 --> 01:39:59,271
She wasn't really a mom.

1441
01:40:01,481 --> 01:40:02,648
Not like that, anyway.

1442
01:40:02,649 --> 01:40:04,734
She was, before we changed.

1443
01:40:04,735 --> 01:40:06,652
Yeah, well, if that's all it takes
for you to stop being a mom,

1444
01:40:06,653 --> 01:40:07,654
then you're not a mom.

1445
01:40:08,572 --> 01:40:10,699
What would you do
if you had daughters like us?

1446
01:40:11,199 --> 01:40:12,284
I'd love them.

1447
01:40:15,871 --> 01:40:17,581
- Especially the redhead one.
- Shut up.

1448
01:40:20,375 --> 01:40:21,752
We have each other.

1449
01:40:25,547 --> 01:40:27,174
And we have ice cream.

1450
01:40:29,051 --> 01:40:30,427
- One mint chip, one chocolate?
- Yeah.

1451
01:40:36,850 --> 01:40:37,851
Okay.

1452
01:40:39,394 --> 01:40:40,979
Now I know how you're playing.

1453
01:40:58,413 --> 01:40:59,497
- Get down!
- Get down!

1454
01:40:59,498 --> 01:41:01,165
- Get down! Get down!
- Get down! Get down!

1455
01:41:01,166 --> 01:41:03,001
- Get down on the ground now!
- Get down! Get down!

1456
01:41:05,420 --> 01:41:06,421
Sara!

1457
01:41:12,010 --> 01:41:13,428
<i>I'm sorry, Jean.</i>

1458
01:41:14,262 --> 01:41:15,722
<i>I have to keep you safe.</i>

1459
01:41:58,265 --> 01:42:01,393
Subject is awake. Heart rate is 94 bpm.

1460
01:42:04,146 --> 01:42:07,733
Jean, that's not gonna work anymore,
thanks to Spider-Man.

1461
01:42:11,194 --> 01:42:12,195
Jean?

1462
01:42:21,747 --> 01:42:23,080
I need you to breathe.

1463
01:42:23,081 --> 01:42:24,750
I need you to look at me and breathe.

1464
01:42:25,292 --> 01:42:26,584
Okay?

1465
01:42:26,585 --> 01:42:28,086
You're safe. Breathe.

1466
01:42:30,672 --> 01:42:31,840
Where is she?

1467
01:42:33,258 --> 01:42:35,259
Like your sister,
you've been blessed with a power

1468
01:42:35,260 --> 01:42:38,055
that has the potential
to do tremendous good in the world,

1469
01:42:38,805 --> 01:42:40,140
or tremendous damage.

1470
01:42:41,099 --> 01:42:45,103
A power like yours in the hands of a child
is an impossible burden.

1471
01:42:45,812 --> 01:42:46,897
But imagine...

1472
01:42:48,023 --> 01:42:50,524
if that power was placed
in the hands of people

1473
01:42:50,525 --> 01:42:51,902
who actually know what to do with it.

1474
01:43:00,911 --> 01:43:02,663
Where is my sister?

1475
01:43:05,540 --> 01:43:07,542
You're gonna change the world, Jean.

1476
01:43:07,918 --> 01:43:08,919
Hey!

1477
01:43:09,670 --> 01:43:10,671
Hey!

1478
01:43:32,526 --> 01:43:33,776
Frank.

1479
01:43:33,777 --> 01:43:35,778
I know where you are, what you're doing.

1480
01:43:35,779 --> 01:43:36,905
<i>Oh, yeah? And how's that?</i>

1481
01:43:37,531 --> 01:43:39,324
I got eyes everywhere, kid.

1482
01:43:40,409 --> 01:43:43,119
Look, Frank.
Damage Control kidnapped Jean's sister.

1483
01:43:43,120 --> 01:43:45,663
Jean was just trying to find her.
We were wrong about everything.

1484
01:43:45,664 --> 01:43:47,082
Sentimental horseshit.

1485
01:43:47,958 --> 01:43:50,126
You've seen what she can do
and what she's capable of.

1486
01:43:50,127 --> 01:43:52,671
What, you're gonna let her loose?
Is that what you're gonna do?

1487
01:43:53,880 --> 01:43:57,384
I'll tell you right now, you do that,
I handle it my way.

1488
01:43:57,884 --> 01:43:59,428
<i>Frank, please, can you just...</i>

1489
01:43:59,720 --> 01:44:00,804
Frank!

1490
01:44:13,400 --> 01:44:14,567
Distance check?

1491
01:44:14,568 --> 01:44:15,901
Forty-foot clearance.

1492
01:44:15,902 --> 01:44:17,403
Locking down the room.

1493
01:44:17,404 --> 01:44:18,405
Locking down.

1494
01:44:23,660 --> 01:44:24,661
<i>Disengage inhibitor.</i>

1495
01:44:29,207 --> 01:44:31,376
<i>Jean, your powers
are now fully operational.</i>

1496
01:44:40,927 --> 01:44:43,764
<i>As you can tell,
we are beyond your jump radius.</i>

1497
01:44:45,182 --> 01:44:46,850
Tell me what V-Max is.

1498
01:44:47,643 --> 01:44:49,686
You're the second person
to ask me about that. I...

1499
01:44:50,395 --> 01:44:51,897
I have no idea what that means.

1500
01:44:52,022 --> 01:44:53,565
<i>She sent me a message.</i>

1501
01:44:54,232 --> 01:44:56,026
She was trying to help me find her.

1502
01:44:57,027 --> 01:45:00,489
She communicated with you telepathically
across all that distance?

1503
01:45:00,906 --> 01:45:03,951
We did register a huge spike
in that session.

1504
01:45:05,786 --> 01:45:06,953
Fascinating.

1505
01:45:06,954 --> 01:45:09,164
What does it mean, asshole?

1506
01:45:10,874 --> 01:45:11,917
I don't know.

1507
01:45:12,876 --> 01:45:14,211
Let's begin.

1508
01:45:22,386 --> 01:45:24,762
<i>Our work with Sara centered on two areas,</i>

1509
01:45:24,763 --> 01:45:27,139
identifying the source of her power

1510
01:45:27,140 --> 01:45:29,476
and identifying a path towards copying it.

1511
01:45:30,519 --> 01:45:34,146
If we could find a way to record
a telepathic brain during a jump,

1512
01:45:34,147 --> 01:45:37,275
then perhaps we could replicate
those pathways

1513
01:45:37,276 --> 01:45:39,027
in a mind of our choosing.

1514
01:45:40,445 --> 01:45:43,573
<i>This instrument is your sister's legacy.</i>

1515
01:45:44,700 --> 01:45:47,577
<i>We built this together
over many months of trial and error.</i>

1516
01:45:48,829 --> 01:45:50,956
I hope you and I can honor her sacrifice.

1517
01:45:54,126 --> 01:45:55,460
What are you talking about?

1518
01:45:56,962 --> 01:45:58,297
Trigger the first jump.

1519
01:46:03,010 --> 01:46:05,594
Tell me what V-Max is.

1520
01:46:05,595 --> 01:46:07,180
I know that's where you're hiding her.

1521
01:46:22,446 --> 01:46:23,447
She's jumping.

1522
01:46:25,741 --> 01:46:26,742
Copy.

1523
01:46:27,284 --> 01:46:30,369
We're in full lockdown.
Process has commenced.

1524
01:46:30,370 --> 01:46:31,371
What process?

1525
01:46:32,831 --> 01:46:35,167
Hey, whoa,
that's a pretty serious look there, dude.

1526
01:46:36,043 --> 01:46:37,668
Hey, hey, whoa! What the hell, man?

1527
01:46:37,669 --> 01:46:39,755
Come on. I'm a friend of Damage Control.
What are you doin'?

1528
01:46:44,301 --> 01:46:45,844
It's gonna be like that. You wanna go.

1529
01:46:45,969 --> 01:46:46,970
All right.

1530
01:46:47,471 --> 01:46:48,972
All right, well, just give me a sec.

1531
01:46:49,514 --> 01:46:50,557
Give me a sec.

1532
01:46:51,391 --> 01:46:52,934
I'm not in high school anymore.

1533
01:46:55,103 --> 01:46:56,687
Do you stretch? You a big stretcher?

1534
01:46:56,688 --> 01:46:58,065
I mean, you should do
in your line of work.

1535
01:46:58,732 --> 01:47:01,860
What about you? You guys stretch?
It's so good for you.

1536
01:47:03,487 --> 01:47:04,488
You ready?

1537
01:47:14,122 --> 01:47:15,123
Watch your head!

1538
01:47:35,018 --> 01:47:36,728
Where is Jean Grey?

1539
01:47:37,813 --> 01:47:39,647
That's jump 26.

1540
01:47:39,648 --> 01:47:40,982
Recordings look good.

1541
01:47:40,983 --> 01:47:42,150
Excuse me, sir.

1542
01:47:43,026 --> 01:47:44,111
We have an intruder.

1543
01:47:49,199 --> 01:47:50,491
You were right.

1544
01:47:50,492 --> 01:47:52,536
She's much stronger than her sister.

1545
01:47:53,537 --> 01:47:54,788
Increase the frequency.

1546
01:47:56,290 --> 01:47:57,624
You're doing very well, Jean.

1547
01:48:45,589 --> 01:48:46,923
<i>Jean?</i>

1548
01:48:51,345 --> 01:48:52,512
Jean, can you hear me?

1549
01:48:58,977 --> 01:48:59,978
Jean?

1550
01:49:04,566 --> 01:49:05,776
You're a murderer.

1551
01:49:08,111 --> 01:49:11,280
Her frequencies are evolving.

1552
01:49:11,281 --> 01:49:12,449
This doesn't make sense.

1553
01:49:13,492 --> 01:49:17,745
The last thing
my sister saw was this room.

1554
01:49:17,746 --> 01:49:20,456
Her brainwaves are somehow
affecting the objects around her.

1555
01:49:20,457 --> 01:49:21,540
Shut it down.

1556
01:49:21,541 --> 01:49:22,833
I'm trying, sir.

1557
01:49:22,834 --> 01:49:23,835
What do you mean you're trying?

1558
01:49:24,336 --> 01:49:29,507
The last thing my sister saw
was this goddamn room!

1559
01:49:29,508 --> 01:49:31,385
- Shut it down!
- I can't, sir.

1560
01:49:32,469 --> 01:49:33,470
Move.

1561
01:49:35,931 --> 01:49:37,849
I can't let you do that, Bill.

1562
01:49:41,561 --> 01:49:45,607
The only hands
that will wield this power...

1563
01:49:46,692 --> 01:49:48,151
are mine.

1564
01:50:13,635 --> 01:50:14,636
What is happening?

1565
01:50:16,013 --> 01:50:17,431
Get inside.

1566
01:50:24,354 --> 01:50:25,355
Wait for me!

1567
01:52:00,826 --> 01:52:02,411
- What...
- What do you want?

1568
01:52:06,123 --> 01:52:09,084
Jean, I'm here to help you.

1569
01:52:10,419 --> 01:52:11,795
You put me here.

1570
01:52:12,462 --> 01:52:16,466
I know, and I'm sorry about Sara,
and I'm sorry that I got it so wrong.

1571
01:52:18,719 --> 01:52:19,802
If you came here

1572
01:52:19,803 --> 01:52:23,056
to save a helpless girl
from Damage Control, you're too late.

1573
01:52:24,141 --> 01:52:26,017
They're the ones who need saving.

1574
01:52:26,018 --> 01:52:27,394
And now...

1575
01:52:27,978 --> 01:52:28,979
so do you.

1576
01:52:31,440 --> 01:52:32,441
Here we go.

1577
01:52:46,955 --> 01:52:48,415
God, that's cool.

1578
01:53:09,478 --> 01:53:11,480
Jean! Jean, please!

1579
01:53:25,827 --> 01:53:27,537
Come on! Come on! Come on!

1580
01:53:48,225 --> 01:53:49,309
What the...

1581
01:53:51,186 --> 01:53:52,269
Isn't it funny

1582
01:53:52,270 --> 01:53:55,815
how your friends from Damage Control
developed a special weapon

1583
01:53:55,816 --> 01:53:57,067
just for you?

1584
01:53:58,360 --> 01:54:01,112
They've got a whole task force ready.

1585
01:54:01,113 --> 01:54:02,948
Just in case you ever get out of line.

1586
01:54:07,536 --> 01:54:08,912
People are monsters.

1587
01:54:13,875 --> 01:54:17,004
You shouldn't trust them
any more than they trust you.

1588
01:54:30,684 --> 01:54:31,934
I'm a little busy, Frank.

1589
01:54:31,935 --> 01:54:33,269
We got a problem, kid.

1590
01:54:33,270 --> 01:54:36,023
<i>She got ahold of everyone
within a kilometer of the island.</i>

1591
01:54:36,607 --> 01:54:37,608
Wait, what?

1592
01:54:43,739 --> 01:54:46,032
Hey, look, if you're gonna do something,
you better do it now.

1593
01:54:46,033 --> 01:54:47,117
I'm trying!

1594
01:55:12,726 --> 01:55:14,226
Kid?

1595
01:55:14,227 --> 01:55:16,021
Shit! Goddamn it.

1596
01:55:49,846 --> 01:55:51,138
My sister died

1597
01:55:51,139 --> 01:55:52,391
in this room,

1598
01:55:53,767 --> 01:55:55,394
surrounded by these men.

1599
01:55:56,728 --> 01:55:57,979
And her only crime

1600
01:55:57,980 --> 01:55:59,564
was that she was special.

1601
01:56:01,400 --> 01:56:02,567
Just like you.

1602
01:56:04,027 --> 01:56:05,237
Just like me.

1603
01:56:07,906 --> 01:56:10,909
People like us
don't get to live a normal life.

1604
01:56:13,912 --> 01:56:17,082
We don't get to have friends or a family.

1605
01:56:19,084 --> 01:56:20,460
Those people are gone.

1606
01:56:23,297 --> 01:56:24,965
That life is over.

1607
01:56:51,158 --> 01:56:53,577
So why don't you just
be honest with yourself?

1608
01:56:56,538 --> 01:56:57,873
Are you Peter Parker?

1609
01:57:00,042 --> 01:57:01,418
Or are you Spider-Man?

1610
01:57:34,409 --> 01:57:35,410
I'm both.

1611
01:59:20,223 --> 01:59:22,267
Jean, please.

1612
01:59:23,560 --> 01:59:24,978
This won't make it right.

1613
01:59:27,147 --> 01:59:29,106
Come on. You're not a killer, Jean.

1614
01:59:29,107 --> 01:59:30,400
You have no idea what I am.

1615
01:59:32,152 --> 01:59:33,779
I know that you loved your sister.

1616
01:59:37,115 --> 01:59:40,159
And I know that losing her
felt like you'd lost everything.

1617
01:59:40,160 --> 01:59:43,121
If you come any closer, he dies!
They all do!

1618
02:00:01,431 --> 02:00:03,015
You know this won't bring her back,
right, Jean?

1619
02:00:03,016 --> 02:00:04,017
You...

1620
02:00:20,659 --> 02:00:22,786
Don't be so sure
I can't get into your mind.

1621
02:00:24,955 --> 02:00:27,207
I'm a lot more powerful
since I last tried.

1622
02:00:37,342 --> 02:00:38,593
Go ahead.

1623
02:00:47,644 --> 02:00:48,645
Hey.

1624
02:00:50,022 --> 02:00:51,023
Hey.

1625
02:00:53,358 --> 02:00:56,987
You think you don't have to listen to me
now that you've got powers?

1626
02:01:01,700 --> 02:01:07,330
You know, this... this whole thing
can get really scary.

1627
02:01:07,331 --> 02:01:08,332
You know that?

1628
02:01:26,975 --> 02:01:28,560
It's already pretty scary.

1629
02:01:29,978 --> 02:01:31,479
Yeah.

1630
02:01:31,480 --> 02:01:34,523
And things can change, like, very quickly,

1631
02:01:34,524 --> 02:01:37,610
in ways that we can't
even imagine right now.

1632
02:01:37,611 --> 02:01:38,778
I know.

1633
02:01:38,779 --> 02:01:39,780
No.

1634
02:01:42,532 --> 02:01:44,242
I don't think you do know.

1635
02:01:46,078 --> 02:01:47,663
What do you mean?

1636
02:01:50,791 --> 02:01:52,501
You're a really special person.

1637
02:01:54,127 --> 02:01:57,005
And I would hope that that will always
make you feel really great about yourself,

1638
02:01:58,131 --> 02:02:01,050
but I know sometimes it doesn't.

1639
02:02:01,051 --> 02:02:03,470
Sometimes, you'll be really lonely.

1640
02:02:07,099 --> 02:02:08,308
And sometimes,

1641
02:02:09,643 --> 02:02:11,144
because you're special,

1642
02:02:13,563 --> 02:02:17,234
people can do dark,
monstrous things to you.

1643
02:02:19,486 --> 02:02:20,570
But...

1644
02:02:22,114 --> 02:02:23,532
this is what I want you to know.

1645
02:02:25,534 --> 02:02:26,785
You're beautiful,

1646
02:02:27,452 --> 02:02:28,995
and the people who love you,

1647
02:02:28,996 --> 02:02:32,833
we love you not because you're special,
we love you because you're you.

1648
02:02:34,960 --> 02:02:36,420
I want you to remember that.

1649
02:02:38,672 --> 02:02:40,674
Even when it feels like
you're totally alone.

1650
02:02:43,677 --> 02:02:45,595
That's your deepest responsibility.

1651
02:02:48,890 --> 02:02:52,144
Never forget that,
no matter how powerful you become.

1652
02:03:08,368 --> 02:03:09,453
Hey.

1653
02:03:25,177 --> 02:03:26,720
I'm sorry about your sister.

1654
02:03:32,017 --> 02:03:33,810
I'm sorry about your aunt.

1655
02:03:37,272 --> 02:03:38,523
Yeah, you would've loved her.

1656
02:03:42,361 --> 02:03:44,279
Just because we've lost someone...

1657
02:03:47,449 --> 02:03:49,451
It doesn't mean we have to do this alone.

1658
02:03:51,495 --> 02:03:54,497
I mean, we can't.

1659
02:03:54,498 --> 02:03:56,124
Trust me, I've been trying.

1660
02:03:59,378 --> 02:04:00,587
It doesn't work.

1661
02:04:05,425 --> 02:04:06,635
Even if that's true...

1662
02:04:11,014 --> 02:04:12,182
I have no one.

1663
02:04:16,895 --> 02:04:17,980
You have me.

1664
02:05:02,608 --> 02:05:03,609
Are you hurt?

1665
02:05:04,067 --> 02:05:05,152
No, I'm fine.

1666
02:05:11,074 --> 02:05:12,075
I'm okay.

1667
02:05:12,993 --> 02:05:14,535
- Peter.
- I'm okay, I'm okay, I'm okay.

1668
02:05:14,536 --> 02:05:15,621
Peter. No.

1669
02:05:19,750 --> 02:05:21,751
Peter, Peter. No, no.

1670
02:05:21,752 --> 02:05:23,545
No, no, no, Peter. Peter.

1671
02:05:24,838 --> 02:05:27,340
Jean, you gotta get outta here.
They'll be looking for you.

1672
02:05:27,341 --> 02:05:29,133
No, no, no, no, no.
Please, just stay with me.

1673
02:05:29,134 --> 02:05:30,468
Come on, hold on. Come on, please!

1674
02:05:30,469 --> 02:05:31,637
Jean, you're...

1675
02:05:32,512 --> 02:05:34,014
You're gonna be okay.

1676
02:05:35,307 --> 02:05:36,308
Just go.

1677
02:05:38,518 --> 02:05:39,519
Look at me.

1678
02:05:57,287 --> 02:06:02,167
<i>Shock today, as Spider-Man arrived
at Bellevue Hospital with a bullet wound,</i>

1679
02:06:02,668 --> 02:06:04,336
<i>seemingly at death's door.</i>

1680
02:06:06,546 --> 02:06:09,256
<i>The reclusive crime fighter
is in critical condition,</i>

1681
02:06:09,257 --> 02:06:12,135
{\an8}<i>as the city's top medical experts
work to save him.</i>

1682
02:06:15,722 --> 02:06:18,475
<i>Tonight, all eyes are on Spider-Man.</i>

1683
02:06:20,519 --> 02:06:22,854
<i>The hero who saved
New York so many times...</i>

1684
02:06:23,355 --> 02:06:25,816
{\an8}<i>is now in the hands
of its best and brightest.</i>

1685
02:06:28,318 --> 02:06:31,280
<i>And the people of New York
hold their breath.</i>

1686
02:07:38,138 --> 02:07:39,139
Frank?

1687
02:07:42,601 --> 02:07:43,769
Where am I?

1688
02:07:45,729 --> 02:07:48,147
- No, no, no, no, no. Hey.
- Where's my mask?

1689
02:07:48,148 --> 02:07:49,523
Don't worry about that. I got you covered.

1690
02:07:49,524 --> 02:07:50,567
Hey, you're good.

1691
02:07:51,068 --> 02:07:52,526
Where's Jean? Is she okay?

1692
02:07:52,527 --> 02:07:54,528
Yeah, she's okay. She's okay.

1693
02:07:54,529 --> 02:07:55,739
Where is she?

1694
02:07:57,032 --> 02:07:58,575
I think maybe she just left.

1695
02:07:59,868 --> 02:08:04,623
She was using her magic voodoo shit
to keep you alive.

1696
02:08:06,124 --> 02:08:08,251
Yeah... she's all right.

1697
02:08:14,925 --> 02:08:15,926
I'm sorry.

1698
02:08:20,806 --> 02:08:22,348
- Frank.
- Just... Just... I'm...

1699
02:08:22,349 --> 02:08:24,100
- Frank, it's okay.
- I'm really sorry for what I did.

1700
02:08:24,101 --> 02:08:25,977
- No, Frank, it's okay.
- And it's... No, it's a lot of things,

1701
02:08:25,978 --> 02:08:27,813
but it sure as shit ain't okay, all right?

1702
02:08:31,483 --> 02:08:32,484
I've seen...

1703
02:08:34,319 --> 02:08:37,906
I've seen real bravery, kid, in my day.

1704
02:08:39,658 --> 02:08:40,659
But that...

1705
02:08:42,119 --> 02:08:43,537
that was something else.

1706
02:08:46,957 --> 02:08:48,374
You crying, Frank?

1707
02:08:48,375 --> 02:08:49,876
No. I ain't...

1708
02:08:56,633 --> 02:08:58,552
You know, you look the exact way
I thought you would.

1709
02:08:59,678 --> 02:09:00,679
You know.

1710
02:09:01,138 --> 02:09:02,306
A nice kid.

1711
02:09:04,808 --> 02:09:06,143
Never had a friend like that.

1712
02:09:07,978 --> 02:09:09,521
Are we friends now?

1713
02:09:16,486 --> 02:09:18,154
I can't believe I just saw you cry.

1714
02:09:18,155 --> 02:09:20,197
I didn't cry. What are you talking about?

1715
02:09:20,198 --> 02:09:21,658
Bullshit.

1716
02:09:23,660 --> 02:09:25,328
Yeah, this.

1717
02:09:25,329 --> 02:09:27,038
They've been doing it all night.

1718
02:09:27,039 --> 02:09:29,583
They've been here since you walked in.
Just take a look.

1719
02:09:40,344 --> 02:09:43,387
Yo, kid, when you came in,
they had to cut through the suit,

1720
02:09:43,388 --> 02:09:45,474
but when you're ready to split...

1721
02:09:46,725 --> 02:09:47,809
I got a plan.

1722
02:10:09,748 --> 02:10:11,667
Hey, it's Spider-Man!

1723
02:10:14,252 --> 02:10:15,671
Spider-Man!

1724
02:10:19,466 --> 02:10:20,550
Hey!

1725
02:10:23,178 --> 02:10:24,596
Yeah, Spider-Man!

1726
02:10:26,014 --> 02:10:27,766
You're the best, Spider-Man!

1727
02:10:28,850 --> 02:10:30,143
Spider-Man!

1728
02:10:31,853 --> 02:10:33,021
Over here!

1729
02:10:34,022 --> 02:10:35,314
Thank you!

1730
02:10:35,315 --> 02:10:36,608
Spider-Man!

1731
02:11:09,391 --> 02:11:13,561
Spider-Man! Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

1732
02:11:13,562 --> 02:11:18,650
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

1733
02:11:28,785 --> 02:11:36,834
Spider-Man! Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

1734
02:11:36,835 --> 02:11:39,212
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

1735
02:12:42,818 --> 02:12:43,819
I've...

1736
02:12:46,822 --> 02:12:48,782
Been thinking a lot about what you said.

1737
02:12:51,326 --> 02:12:54,037
And you'd be happy to know
that I've decided I'm not...

1738
02:12:55,706 --> 02:12:57,708
I'm not gonna do this alone anymore.

1739
02:13:07,217 --> 02:13:08,468
I miss you, May.

1740
02:13:16,893 --> 02:13:18,978
I mean, I've still got a little pain
in my back,

1741
02:13:18,979 --> 02:13:22,023
but I could probably get back out there
if you need me for anything.

1742
02:13:22,024 --> 02:13:24,567
<i>No. What I need you to do is rest.</i>

1743
02:13:24,568 --> 02:13:26,694
I know, I know, but come on,
you gotta give me something.

1744
02:13:26,695 --> 02:13:28,696
